hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19039","(19039) Ibn al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Hisham, that his father divorced him, so he had the same wife."
"19040","(19040) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah, that he was divorced and he enjoyed his marriage. With a newborn"
"19041","(19041) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he enjoyed his child."
"19042","(19042) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: I raise the burden. The servant, then below that: clothing, then below that: maintenance."
"19043","(19043) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr ibn Shu’aib, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: He placed al-Mu’ta’i The dress was lifted by the servant."
"19044","(19044) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Among the average comfort items are armor, a veil, and a veil."
"19045","(19045) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, regarding the belongings of a divorced woman: her clothes in her home, the armor and the veil. And the quilt and the robe."
"19046","(19046) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: People used to enjoy themselves, and among them were those who enjoyed serving people. And among them were some who used to give the two hundred, and among them were those who gave the armor and the veil and the blanket, and among them were those who He gives the maintenance."
"19047","(19047) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Ayyub, who said: Aqeel narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab. He said: The highest is the servant, then the clothing, then the maintenance."
"19048","(19048) Muhammad bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The woman who is mustahaadah should take care of the relatives."
"19049","(19049) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ruh bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, who said: “You should observe the waiting period.” With the readers."
"19050","(19050) Abbad bin Al-Awwam narrated to us, on the authority of Ruh bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, who said: Tawoos said: She should observe the fasts of fasting."
"19051","(19051) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Raja’, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Ata’ that they said: Al-Muṣṭhaḍah. She takes pride in her peers."
"19052","(19052) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Ata’, al-Hakam, and al-Hasan regarding al-Mustahadha. They said: She will count the days of her reading."
"19053","(19053) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: You should consider the Qara’i."
"19054","(19054) Muhammad bin Musaar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Taman, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The woman who undergoes menstruation should observe the waiting period. With the readers."
"19055","(19055) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: If a man divorces the woman who undergoes menstruation, then the third woman undergoes menstruation. As long as she is menstruating, her husband should not have the right to take her back, nor should she wash herself or pray, until she has had more sexual intercourse than She was menstruating."
"19056","(19056) Hammad bin Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Count the mustahadah Sunnah"
"19057","(19057) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said, “Among the doubts of the woman who is suffering from istihaadah and the woman who does not She will menstruate twice during the month, and three times during the months. Her number is three months. He said: So he was his leader. That's his opinion."
"19058","(19058) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Abi Wahshiy, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zaid, who said: Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar remembered the missing woman, and they both said: Wait for four years, then her husband’s guardian will divorce her. Then they waited for four months and ten, then they discussed spending, and Ibn Umar said: She has the right to spend on his wealth by detaining herself. For his reason, Ibn Abbas said: Not like that, then you are being unfair to the heirs, but we are taking from him his wealth, so if he gives That is her right over his wealth, otherwise there is nothing left for her."
"19059","(19059) Abdullah bin Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, On the authority of Sulaiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit, who said: If a woman with childbirth is divorced, that blood does not count as the waiting period."
"19060","(19060) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He was asked about a woman in postpartum condition: Does she observe the postpartum period? He said: Do not observe her breathing."
"19061","(19061) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If she is divorced while she is married, her blood is not considered a waiting period. Her postpartum period during her waiting period."
"19062","(19062) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Qays bin Saad, on the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj. On the authority of Sulaiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, who said: If a man divorces his wife while she is pregnant, the blood of her postpartum blood is not considered a waiting period. I counted it"
"19063","(19063) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Al-Harith, who said: The woman who is in need of menstruation can make sure that she A mustaḥaḥ if her menstrual period has passed the last period for which women purify themselves."
"19064","(19064) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hikam. He said: If a recitation overtakes another recitation, then it is mustahaadah."
"19065","(19065) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Qur’a The pure ones"
"19066","(19066) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, who said: Al-Qasim and Salem used to say: The pure Aqra’ are the pure ones."
"19067","(19067) Ibn Abi Ghaniyā told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: The menstruating Aqra’."
"19068","(19068) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The number of the mother of the child is three menstruation."
"19069","(19069) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Three menstrual cycles."
"19070","(19070) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj and Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali, who said: Three menstrual cycles."
"19071","(19071) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Ali, similar to him."
"19072","(19072) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali and Abdullah, who said: Three menstrual cycles if He died from her."
"19073","(19073) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Three Quran narrators."
"19074","(19074) Abd al-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Raja` ibn Hiyawah, on the authority of Qubaisa, on the authority of Amr ibn Al-Aas said: Do not confuse the Sunnah of our Prophet with us. Her iddah is the same as the iddah of her husband who has died. (Abu Dawud 2302. Abu Ali 7300)"
"19075","(19075) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Fadalah bin Ubaid, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh, on the authority of Abu I'd add that they said: Her waiting period if her husband dies is the same number as a free woman."
"19076","(19076) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The count is the mother of the child if her husband dies. Four months and ten days."
"19077","(19077) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Sa’id bin Jubair that they both said: Idah is the mother of the child if Her master passed away after four months and ten days."
"19078","(19078) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: Al-Hakam bin Utaiba asked Al-Zuhri about the iddah of the child’s mother if he died. Her master narrated it, and he said: The Sunnah, and he said: What is the Sunnah? He said: Breeira was freed, so she used the waiting period for a free woman.\n(Ibn Majah 2007, Bayhaqi 251)"
"19079","(19079) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The number of the child’s mother is four. Months and tens."
"19080","(19080) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, And Saeed bin Al-Musayyab is like that."
"19081","(19081) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ali, like that."
"19082","(19082) Hafs bin Ghayath and Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: I counted it."
"19083","(19083) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: The number of the child’s mother if her master dies"
"19084","(19084) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he used to say: Her waiting period is menstrual when he dies on her behalf. Her master"
"19085","(19085) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Salim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Zayd, who said: Her waiting period is menstruation."
"19086","(19086) Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Her waiting period is menstruation."
"19087","(۱۹۰۸۷) حَدَّثَنَا حَفْصٌ، عَنْ إسْمَاعِیلَ، عَنِ الشَّعْبِیِّ قَالَ: عِدَّتُہَا حَیْضَۃٌ فَلِمَ لاَ تُوَرِّثُونَہَا إذَا جَعَلْتُمُوہَا ثَلاَثَ menstruation"
"19088","(19088) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’ and Tawus, who said: He counted the mother of the child and the concubine if he died. Its master has two months and five nights."
"19089","(19089) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, who said: I heard Al-Qasim and it was mentioned to him that Abd al-Malik bin Marwan Separate between men and women who are mothers of children who were married after one or two menstrual cycles, until they have observed the waiting period for four days. A month or ten, and he said: Glory be to God. God says in His Book: {And those of you who die and leave behind wives}"
"19090","(19090) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, that Amr bin Al-Aas was the mother of a son She was freed to observe the waiting period for three menstrual periods. He wrote to Omar and he wrote to improve her opinion."
"19091","(19091) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he used to say: If he frees her, then her waiting period is three menstrual cycles."
"19092","(19092) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, who said: When he frees her, or dies on her behalf, then I will wait for her. Three menstrual periods."
"19093","(19093) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: If a man frees the mother of his children, she must observe the waiting period with two menstrual cycles: And he said: Al-Zuhri: Three reciters."
"19094","(19094) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr, who said: Jabir bin Zaid was asked about a man who frees his concubine. And it is true that the waiting period is three menstrual cycles if she is menstruating, and if she is not menstruating then her waiting period is three months if Someone else married her."
"19095","(19095) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar that he used to say: I have prepared her. Menstruation if he frees her, or dies from her."
"19096","(19096) Ali bin Musahir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Habib Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali: Iddah Al-Ummah Two menstrual periods, and if she does not menstruate, then a month and a half."
"19097","(19097) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The number of women’s menstrual cycles is two menstrual cycles. If she does not menstruate, then a month and a half."
"19098","(19098) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, the same."
"19099","(19099) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Qays, who said: I asked Salim bin Abdullah about the waiting period for female mothers, and he said: Two menstruation periods. If she does not menstruate, then a month and a half."
"19100","(19100) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The number of slave women is two menstrual cycles."
"19101","(19101) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If she menstruates, then two menstrual cycles, and if she is among those who do not She menstruates for a month and a half."
"19102","(19102) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The number of mothers. Two menstruation, if she is menstruating, and if she is not menstruating, then a month and a half."
"19103","(19103) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, he heard Amr ibn Aws say: A man from Thaqif told me, saying: I heard Omar Ibn Al-Khattab said: If I were able to make the number of dead women one and a half menstruation, I would do so. A man said to him: If I made it a month And a half and remained silent."
"19104","(19104) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: The number of women’s menstrual cycles is two menstrual cycles, if they do not menstruate. Fasharaan."
"19105","(19105) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak regarding the mother who had not menstruated and had lost her menstruation: Her iddah is forty-five days. If she is menstruating, then her iddah is menstruation."
"19106","(19106) Abu Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; Regarding the waiting period for a mother, he said: If she is menstruating, then two menstrual cycles, and if she is not menstruating, then her waiting period is forty-five days."
"19107","(19107) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: The number of a slave woman is equal to half the number of a free woman."
"19108","(19108) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, regarding a slave woman who has intercourse: if she is sold, or She was given away, or was emancipated, so let her be cleansed by her menstruation."
"19109","(19109) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, regarding slave mothers when they are freed. He said: I have numbered them. Three menstrual periods."
"19110","(19110) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali, regarding a slave woman who is freed. He said: The waiting period is three days. It was read."
"19111","(19111) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: If a mother is freed, she must wait for two menstrual periods, and he said: Al-Zuhri: Three reciters."
"19112","(19112) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: She must wait for three menstrual periods."
"19113","(19113) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered Burayra to The waiting period for a free woman."
"19114","(19114) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Burayra had observed the waiting period of a free woman."
"19115","(19115) Ismail Ibn Aliyya narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Burayra was freed, so she followed his waiting period. The heat"
"19116","(19116) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, that the mother was divorced twice, and his freedmen did not catch her. Before it expires, he said: The waiting period for a mother should be observed."
"19117","(19117) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If she is divorced once, then her emancipator takes her back before When her waiting period has ended, she is considered to be the waiting period for a free woman, and if she has divorced two times, then she is freed, then she has waited for her to wait for it. The mother when she has died, and the same for the deceased."
"19118","(19118) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he said: If a man divorces his wife and he is his mother He said: No. He would marry her until he married another husband, and her waiting period would be the same as his mother."
"19119","(19119) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Ali bin al-Hakam, on the authority of al-Dahhak about the illiterate. She was divorced twice, then she was freed during her waiting period. He said: She is in the waiting period for two menstrual periods, and if she divorced once, then she is freed during her waiting period. Her waiting period. He said: She is waiting for three menstrual periods, and her husband has more right to her."
"19120","(19120) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab that he said: I counted it as he did. The heat"
"19121","(19121) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Amer, who said: If the mothers are divorced Two divorces, then she is freed at that time, and her waiting period is the same as the number of mothers. If she is divorced once, then she is freed at that time. So I counted it as a free woman."
"19122","(19122) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, regarding a woman whose husband died, then She was set free. He said: She fulfills the waiting period of the slave woman, and she has nothing but the waiting period of the slave woman."
"19123","(19123) Omar bin Zur’a told us, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that he used to say: If her husband dies She is a slave, so emancipation has overtaken her, and she is in her waiting period, so she will complete four months and ten days."
"19124","(19124) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Salih Ibn Muslim, who said: I said to Al-Sha’biyy: A man divorced his wife, then another came. So he married her? Omar said: He will separate them, and she will complete her first iddah, and she will complete a new iddah from this, and the friendship will be kept in the house. Money, and the second will never marry her, and the first will become a suitor, and Ali said: He will separate her from her husband. She will complete her first waiting period, and she will observe a new waiting period after that, and the dowry will be given to her for what was permissible from her private parts. And they both will become suitors."
"19125","(19125) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Ibrahim and Al-Shu’abi regarding a woman. She got married during her waiting period. Al-Sha’bi said: She resumes three recitations and completes what remains from the first, and Ibrahim said: You complete what remains from the first and resume three recitations."
"19126","(19126) Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyā told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: It is distinguished between them, and she will complete her waiting period from the first, and she will wait for the last one, and she will have the dowry with what was permissible from her private parts, so if Her waiting period has expired, so let her marry him, or someone else if she wants."
"19127","(19127) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ali; Concerning a man who marries a mother who has a child by someone else and dies. He said: He should not be near her until it becomes clear to him what is in her womb. , or menstruating."
"19128","(19128) Yahya bin Zakariya told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Omar, who said: No. He brought it near until he saw whether there was a rope on it or not."
"19129","(19129) Yahya bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hassan bin Al-Mukhariq, that Al-Hasan bin Ali said: No. He will approach her until she completes the waiting period, or he said: until she has menstruated."
"19130","(19130) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, that Al-Hasan ibn Ali prayed over my funeral and said to the husband: And the woman has a child from someone else: you do not have the right to claim a share that is not yours."
"19131","(19131) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim and Ammar, who said: He should not approach it until it is clear whether it is pregnant or not."
"19132","(19132) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He should not approach her until she has fully menstruated."
"19133","(19133) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id and Al-Hasan. They said: Omar ibn Al-Khattab postponed If he is able to do so, he will separate them, otherwise he will have to separate them, and she will have to do the waiting period."
"19134","(19134) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: When the year has passed, she must observe the waiting period after the year. The divorced woman, even if he did not divorce her."
"19135","(19135) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the woman of the two eyes, he said: She must wait for it if he separates them."
"19136","(19136) Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: On her. The number"
"19137","(19137) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Kathir, Abi al-Sabbah, who said: I said to Sa`id bin al-Musayyab: How long should his wife wait? Meaning the apostate. He said: Three recitations. I said: So if he is killed? He said: Four months and ten days."
"19138","(19138) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Sha’bi and al-Hakam, who said: Concerning a Muslim man who abandons Islam and goes to the enemy’s land. They said: His wife shall observe the waiting period of three menstrual cycles if she is menstruating, and if If she does not menstruate, then three months, and if she is pregnant, she may give birth, then get married if she wants, and if he comes back So he repented before her waiting period was over, so that their marriage would continue."
"19139","(19139) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: If a man apostatizes from Islam, then it has become clear. His wife divorced him with an irrevocable divorce, and she has no recourse if he comes back, and she must observe the waiting period of the divorced woman."
"19140","(19140) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He has more right to her as long as she is in The waiting period, if he returns while he is in her waiting period, then it is his wife. Abu Ma’shar said: So Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to him about that. Abdul Hamid bin Abdul Rahman in the apostate."
"19141","(19141) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, who said: I asked al-Sha`bi about a woman. A dhimmi woman was divorced and became Muslim during her waiting period. He said: If she became Muslim during her waiting period, then she is bound to Islam as is binding on Muslim women."
"19142","(19142) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurri, who said: Al-Hasan was asked about my Christianity under another’s Christianity, so I converted to Islam, and he separated. Between them? He said: Yes, he said: She has a waiting period. He said: Yes, she has a waiting period of three menstruation, or three months."
"19143","(19143) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, who said: Ata was asked about a woman whose husband dies while... Christian, then she becomes Muslim. How long should she wait? He said: Four months and ten days."
"19144","(19144) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: Divorce of a Jewish woman. Christianity is the divorce of a Muslim woman, and her waiting period is the same as the free Muslim woman."
"19145","(19145) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, and Al-Hasan was among those He marries a Jewish woman or a Christian woman over a Muslim woman. He said: He will divide between them equally, and her divorce will be a free divorce. I promised her that."
"19146","(19146) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: The divorce of a Jew and a Christian is a divorce. The free woman and her iddah are the iddah of the free woman and he divides to them just as he divides to the free woman."
"19147","(19147) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The number of Christians is the same as the number of The Muslim woman and her division are the same."
"19148","(19148) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amer; Concerning a man who marries a Muslim woman, a Jewish woman, or a Christian woman. He said: He makes it equal between them regarding the division of his wealth. And himself"
"19149","(19149) Shababi told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who marries a Christian woman, and they said: I divided them equally."
"19150","(19150) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Abdi, on the authority of Ali, who said: If she gives birth to a son and he survives... There is a child in her womb, so he has more right to her as long as she does not give birth to the other."
"19151","(19151) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’ bin Misra, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If she gives birth to a child If a child remains in her womb, he has more right to take her back as long as she does not give birth to the other."
"19152","(19152) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’ like him."
"19153","(19153) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, And Ata and Suleiman bin Yassar; In a man who divorces his wife once, and she gives birth to a child, and there is another in her womb, and her husband returns to her between them. That is why they said: If he wishes, he can take her back until she gives birth to the other of them."
"19154","(19154) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, regarding a man who divorced his wife and... She has two children in her womb. He said, “He has more right to take her back as long as she does not give birth to the other,” and he recited: “And those who are pregnant. Their term is that they give birth to their own children.”"
"19155","(19155) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Zuhri, regarding the one who divorces while in her womb there are two children. He said He has the right to return until she loses what is in her stomach."
"19156","(19156) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said, “He has more right to her as long as she does not give birth to the other.”"
"19157","(19157) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, al-Hasan, and Suleiman bin Yasar. And Ata bin Abi Rabah said: He has more right to her as long as she does not abandon the other."
"19158","(19158) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amir, who said: They used to say: If there was one son, he would go out. A group of them was the king of the Raj'a unless all of it came out."
"19159","(19159) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hanzali, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He has more right to her unless You put the other down."
"19160","(19160) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man dies, or divorces his wife, She is pregnant and gave birth to a boy and another remained in her womb, so her waiting period for the first had ended."
"19161","(19161) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If one of them gives birth, then she becomes void."
"19162","(19162) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: If you put on the first, then it has stopped. He said: It was said to him: Will he get married? He said: No. His leaders said: The servant’s opponent."
"19163","(19163) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A divorced woman shall observe the waiting period in her husband’s house, and shall not use kohl. With beautiful eyeliner."
"19164","(19164) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: A man came to Abdullah and said: I have divorced my wife three times, and she wants to leave. He said: Lock her up. He said: Do not sit. He said: Tie her up. He said: She has brothers. He stiffened their necks and said: Be prepared, the prince."
"19165","(19165) Jarir told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, who said: A divorced woman may visit but not spend the night."
"19166","(19166) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: A woman who has been divorced on three occasions must not leave her husband’s house or touch perfume except when purifying herself by removing her hair and nails."
"19167","(19167) Abu Zukair Yahya bin Muhammad al-Qurashi told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Nadli, who said: I divorced my three-year-old cousin, so I came to Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab to ask him, and he said: She should observe the waiting period in her husband’s house where she was divorced. He said: I asked Al-Qasim, Salim, Abu Bakr bin Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Harith, and Kharijah bin Zaid and Suleiman bin Saar, and they all spoke to me. He says something like Saeed."
"19168","(19168) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri regarding a woman who was divorced three times and whose husband died: They shall observe the waiting period in their husband’s house and have the same marriage."
"19169","(19169) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim, that Yahya bin Saeed bin Al-Aas divorced His wife, the daughter of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hakam, went to her family and sent Aisha to Marwan: Fear God and respond. The woman went home, and Marwan said: Indeed, Abd al-Rahman has defeated me."
"19170","(19170) Abdullah told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Neither the dead nor the deceased shall spend the night. She is free from her husband except in her home until her waiting period is over."
"19171","(19171) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, who said: A woman was divorced in Medina, so the jurists were asked. The people of Medina said: She stays in her house, so Saeed was asked: He said: She stays."
"19172","(19172) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: Fatima bint Qais said: O Messenger By God, I fear that he will attack me. He said: So he ordered her to turn around. (Muslim 1121. Ibn Majah 2033)"
"19173","(19173) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the divorced woman, three times: she may observe the waiting period in a place other than her home if she wishes."
"19174","(19174) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Habib who said: I asked Ata’ and he said: She may observe the waiting period wherever she wants, and Al-Hasan said this. Also"
"19175","(19175) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Fatima bint Qays, who said: I wrote That is one of the letters in her. She said: I was with a man from Banu Makhzum and he divorced me out of hand. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Go to Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is a man whose sight has lost, and if you put anything in it, he will not see anything.\n(Muslim 1116. Abu Dawud 2278)"
"19176","(19176) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, he was asked about a woman who was divorced while he was living with her. In a house with a renter, and he said: If it is good, he will give her a wage and she will remain in her house until her waiting period is over."
"19177","(19177) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, who said: Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab was asked about a woman who was divorced. And she is in a house that is rented to whom? He said: On her husband."
"19178","(19178) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, that Omar returned the needy women, or the women who had performed Umrah who had gone out in their waiting period."
"19179","(19179) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Hamid al-Araj, on the authority of Mujahid, that Omar and Uthman returned to Hajj or They performed Umrah to the point of staying in their homes."
"19180","(19180) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Ibn Masoud rejected women who were performing Hajj or Umrah. They went out in their Iddah."
"19181","(19181) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Miqdam, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The deceased A divorced woman does not perform Hajj, does not perform Umrah, and does not wear a bodysuit."
"19182","(19182) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, that Ibn Umar rebuked a woman. She performs Hajj during her waiting period."
"19183","(19183) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Omar ibn Al-Khattab returned women from Dhul-Halifah is a woman whose husbands were killed in some of those waters."
"19184","(19184) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Humaid bin Qais, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said: The age of the Bedouin wives of the deceased women rejected their husbands, so they were prevented from performing Hajj."
"19185","(19185) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Asama, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Ata’ that Aisha performed the Hajj Kulthum in her waiting period."
"19186","(19186) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas that he saw no harm in divorced women. Thirdly, their husbands who have died must perform Hajj during their waiting period."
"19187","(19187) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Habib Al-Mu’allim, who said: I asked Ata’ about a woman who was divorced three times and the one who died from her: Tahjan. About them in their waiting period? He said: Yes, and Habib said: Al-Hasan used to say the same thing."
"19188","(19188) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Zainab bint Ka’b bin Ajra, and she was under Ubay’s wife. Saeed Al-Khudri said that his subsidiary sister, Ibn Malik, said: My husband went out to seek treatment for him, and he caught them on the verge of arrival. So they killed him, and my husband’s obituary came while I was in one of the Ansar’s houses, far away from my family’s house. So I came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted me, and I said: O Messenger of God, my husband’s obituary came to me while I was in a vast house, far from the house of my family and the house of my brothers, and he did not He leaves no money to be spent on me, nor the wealth of my heirs, nor a house of his own. If you decide to call the call to prayer, then join my family’s house, and go home. My brothers, for he is dearer to me and brings some of my affairs to me. He said: So do it if you wish. She said: So Qara’ayn came out when God decided on the tongue of His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, to the point that when I was in the mosque, or in some room, he called me and said: How did you claim? She said: So she told him the story. He said: Stay in your house where your husband’s obituary was, until the letter is reached. For his sake, she said: So she observed her waiting period for four months and ten days. (Tirmidhi 1204, Abu Dawud 2294)"
"19189","(19189) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya that a woman from Hamdan was killed. About their wives, and Abdullah said: They meet during the day and spend the night in their homes."
"19190","(19190) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He died leaving some of his wives from Madan, whose husbands So they wanted to gather in the house of one of their women to observe the waiting period, so they sent to Ibn Masoud to ask him. He said: Everyone should observe the waiting period. A woman in her home."
"19191","(19191) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Yusuf ibn Mahak, on the authority of his mother Masikah, that a woman visited She was in a state of labor, so she labored with them, so they sent you to Othman after he had prayed the evening prayer and gone to bed, and I said: Indeed So-and-so visited her family, and she is in her waiting period, and she is in labor, so what do you command her? He said: So he ordered her to be carried home in that state."
"19192","(19192) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ibn Thawban that A woman whose husband died and was too old, so she asked Omar to come to her family? So he granted her permission to come to her family in the whiteness of her day."
"19193","(19193) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman A woman from the Ansar, whose husband died on her behalf, asked Zayd ibn Thabit, but he did not grant her permission except in the middle of her day. Or its night."
"19194","(19194) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A woman was observing the waiting period for her husband, and he died on her behalf. Then her father complained, so she sent to Umm Salama to ask her: Should she come to her father and nurse him? She said: If you are at one end of the day in your house."
"19195","(19195) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, who said: I heard Abraham say: The husband of a woman whose husband has died should not spend the night overnight. Other than her home."
"19196","(19196) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Nafi`, that a woman whose husband died, so she observed the waiting period in a state other than She stayed at home one day, and Ibn Umar ordered her to make up for it."
"19197","(19197) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: I asked my father about her husband who died. Are you moving? He said: No, unless her family moves and she moves with them."
"19198","(19198) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Khasif, who said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab about her husband who died. Does she leave her house? He said: No."
"19199","(19199) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam. He said: Omar and Abdullah used to say: Do not move."
"19200","(19200) Abd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Abdullah’s companions used to say: Do not go out until She died at her husband's house."
"19201","(19201) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, that a woman from the Ansar Her husband died, and her father complained, so she asked Omar’s permission, but he did not give her permission except during the night."
"19202","(19202) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Awf ibn Abi Jamila, who said: A friend of mine died and left him. They planted some groves for him, and his wife came and said: Ask Ibn Umar, should I go out and stand up for him? So I came to Ibn Umar and he said: You will go out during the day and do not spend the night."
"19203","(19203) Zayd ibn Harun told us: Ibn Aoun informed us, on the authority of Anas ibn Sirin, that his son was Abdullah ibn Omar, her husband died, so she came to them and wanted to spend the night with them, but Abdullah bin Omar prevented her and said: Go back to your house. So my house is in it."
"19204","(19204) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: Ali narrated Umm Kulthum when Umar was killed Her sister Aisha moved when Talha was killed."
"19205","(19205) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Graduation."
"19206","(19206) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’ and Abu Al-Sha’athi regarding the deceased, who said: She graduated."
"19207","(19207) Muhammad bin Maysar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir. They both said: The deceased must observe her husband wherever she wishes."
"19208","(19208) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Ali was transporting the deceased from her. Her husband"
"19209","(19209) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Ash-Shabi that Ali transferred Umm Kulthum after seven years."
"19210","(19210) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, regarding a man who divorced his wife and she had her menstruation. A menstrual period, or two menstrual cycles, and she got married during her waiting period, and her waiting period ended with her husband, and he said: She has finished her period. By divorcing him."
"19211","(19211) Abdul-Ala told us, saying: Saeed was asked about a man who married a woman during her waiting period, then he learned that he had married her. In her waiting period, and her waiting period has ended with him, is it for her first husband to take her back? So he told us on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hakam, On the authority of Muhammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, that he said: He will separate them and he will not go back to her because her waiting period has passed. It ended at this point."
"19212","(19212) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, that he said: Her husband has more right to her, and he should not even be close to her. Her waiting period has ended."
"19213","(19213) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, regarding a man who divorced his wife once, Or she was divorced twice and she had two menstrual cycles, then a man married her and she had two menstrual cycles. He said: She became clear from the beginning. And it will not be taken into account for those after him."
"19214","(19214) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: You will be rewarded for it."
"19215","(19215) Ismail Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If her husband died on her behalf, meaning the mother. The waiting period is two months and five nights."
"19216","(19216) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The number of mothers when he dies She and her husband are entitled to half the waiting period of a free month and five days."
"19217","(19217) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, about a Mamluk in which he died. Her husband is free, so her waiting period is two months and five days."
"19218","(19218) Shababi told us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Bukair, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab and Ibn Qusayt regarding the Ummah: So Her husband died, free, so her waiting period was two months and five days."
"19219","(19219) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of alcohol in the case of a mother: If her husband dies, she must observe the waiting period. The heat"
"19220","(19220) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yassar, that Muawiyah asked Zayd bin Thabit said: If she is stabbed during the third menstruation, then she is free from it."
"19221","(19221) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Musa bin Shaddad, on the authority of Omar bin Thabit, who said: Zaid was Ibn Thabit says: If a divorced woman has her third menstruation before her husband takes her back, then he has no right to take her back."
"19222","(19222) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman that Aisha Moreover, they used to say: If it enters into the third bleeding, then there is no right to take it back."
"19223","(19223) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar and Zayd bin Thabit that they said: If she menstruates the third time, then she has passed."
"19224","(19224) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Aban bin Othman and Salem bin Abdullah, who said: If she enters the third menstrual period, she has become clear."
"19225","(19225) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Sulaiman ibn Yasar, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: If She entered her third menstruation, and she has stopped."
"19226","(19226) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Amr, and Abdullah that they said: Whoever divorces His wife has more right to take her back as long as she does not perform ghusl after her third menstruation."
"19227","(19227) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali and Ibn Abbas, who said: He has more right to her as long as he does not She takes a bath after her third menstruation."
"19228","(19228) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Omar, and Abdullah that they said: He has more right to it."
"19229","(19229) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Omar, and Abdullah, they said: He is more worthy. Until she performs ghusl after the third menstruation."
"19230","(19230) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ubaidullah Al-Kala’i, on the authority of an unknown person that Abu Bakr, Omar, Ali, and Ibn Masoud, Abu Al-Darda', Ubadah bin Al-Samit, and Abdullah bin Qais Al-Ash'ari used to say: Concerning a man who divorces his wife once, or twice: He has more right to her as long as she does not perform ghusl after her third menstruation. He inherits from her and she inherits from her as long as she is within the waiting period."
"19231","(19231) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Ubaid, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Omar said: If he enters her The one who has bathed before she pours water over her is more worthy of it. (Saeed bin Mansour 1223)"
"19232","(19232) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ali, who said: He has more right to her. Until she performs ghusl after the third menstruation."
"19233","(19233) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: If only a man He came in to his wife while she was bathing and said: I went back to you and she said: You lied. You lied, and pouring water on her head was more deserving. With it"
"19234","(19234) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Muzahim, that a woman married a young man and he divorced her. One divorce, or two divorces. He said: So he came to her while she was taking a bath after the third menstruation, and he said: O so-and-so, I have I checked with you, and she said: You lied, that is not up to you. So they went to Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, and with him was Abdullah Ibn Masoud, so Omar said: : What do you see, Abu Abdul Rahman? He said: So he said: I adjure you by God, would you have slapped him with water? She said: What she did. He said: So he said: Take her by the hand."
"19235","(19235) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Hakam, that Abu Kanaf divorced his wife but did not He informed her, so he witnessed her return, but he did not inform her. He said: Then Omar said to him: If you catch her before you get married, then you have more right. With it"
"19236","(19236) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of the ruling, he said: Ali said: When he divorced her, then he testified that she would return. Whether he informed her about his wife, or whether he did not teach her."
"19237","(19237) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Umayr bin Yazid, who said: I was sitting at Shurayh: Then a man came and was disputing with his wife, and she said: He divorced me, and he did not inform me about taking me back until she had completed her waiting period and I got married and he had consummation with me. My husband, and Shurayh said: Didn’t you teach her about taking back the same way you taught her about divorce? He did not return it to her."
"19238","(19238) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zaid, who said: If he divorced her, then he did not inform her. By taking her back until the waiting period is over and she gets married and the second husband consummates the marriage with her, then there is nothing wrong with her."
"19239","(19239) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who divorced his wife, then took her back and concealed the reconciliation until her waiting period had ended. He said: If he took her back before he He gets married and has more right to her, otherwise he is lost."
"19240","(19240) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; That Abu Kanf divorced his wife, then he traveled and went back to her, and he wrote to her about that, and he bore witness to that, but he did not The decree reached her until the period of time had passed, so she married the woman. So he rode to Omar, and he told him the story and said: You I have more right to her as long as he does not have intercourse with her."
"19241","(19241) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Ali used to say: He Is he more entitled to it, whether he entered it with it, or whether he did not enter it."
"19242","(19242) Abduh told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Omar, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he used to see that."
"19243","(19243) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ismail narrated to us, saying: I heard Al-Hakam bin Utaiba mentioning, on the authority of Abu Kanf. He divorced his wife, then took her back and did not inform her about taking him back, so she got married, so he went on about that until Omar and said: Go back. She found that she had not gone to her husband to whom she had been married to your wife, so he returned and did not find her. She went to her husband and he took her."
"19244","(19244) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, about a man who divorced His wife, then he sent for her to take her back, but the return did not come to her until she got married. He said: She has ceased to have intercourse with him, even if she overtakes her. Taking him back before he marries his wife."
"19245","(19245) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: If he reviewed Himself is nothing."
"19246","Abu Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shayba told us, he said:\n(19246) Ismail bin Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub, who said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr, Mujahid, and Ata’ about the deceased. About her husband, from what day should she observe the waiting period? They said: From the day he dies. He said: And I heard Ikrimah, Nafi’, and Muhammad bin Sirin say: I have prepared it from the day he dies. Talaq bin Habib: from the day he dies."
"19247","(19247) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. He said: The day he dies."
"19248","(19248) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The number of days from the day of death And he divorces."
"19249","(19249) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Her waiting period has been since the day he divorced her and from The day he dies from her."
"19250","(19250) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, Ibn Sirin, and Abu Al-Aliyah, they said: The number of On the day he dies and from the day he divorces, whoever eats any of the inheritance, it will be his share."
"19251","(19251) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: A woman observes the waiting period for her husband. He has been absent since the day he dies, or since the day he is divorced."
"19252","(19252) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul and Al-Zuhri, who said: A woman observes the waiting period from the day he dies, or He divorced"
"19253","(19253) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The iddah falls from the day he dies and the day he speaks. By divorce"
"19254","(19254) Ibn Aliyah told us on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: From the day he dies."
"19255","(19255) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: She should observe the waiting period from the day her husband died from her."
"19256","(19256) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, who said: Jabir bin Zayd said: From the day he dies, or is divorced."
"19257","(19257) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said from the day he died or was divorced."
"19258","(19258) Waki’ told us, and Yahya bin Adam, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Zaid, On the authority of Abdullah, he said: The number of days is from the day he dies, and the day he is divorced."
"19259","(19259) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Zaid, who said: The number of days from the day he dies and is divorced."
"19260","(19260) Ismail Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam that Ali said: From the day the news came to her."
"19261","(19261) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: From the day he came to her The news"
"19262","(19262) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: She will observe the waiting period from the day the news came to her."
"19263","(19263) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of his followers, who said: From the day the news came to her."
"19264","(19264) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: From the day the news came to her."
"19265","(19265) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Khalas; Concerning a man who divorces his wife while he is absent from her. They said: She shall observe the waiting period from the day the news comes to her."
"19266","(19266) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: If the witnesses testify to divorce or death So I prepared it from that day."
"19267","(19267) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The husband of the deceased, if he was absent from the day of his death, if witnesses testify to this."
"19268","(19268) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: I heard al-Hakam saying: I asked Sa’id ibn Jubayr, about When does her husband die while he is absent? On what day should she observe the waiting period? He said: From the day her husband died, she observes the waiting period if the relationship is established, and if she is divorced, the same applies to that."
"19269","(19269) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: She should observe the waiting period from the day he died, or He will be divorced when clear evidence is established."
"19270","(19270) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab and Sulayman bin Saar that they They said: She must observe the waiting period from the day he died, or he divorced once the relationship is established."
"19271","(19271) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: She should observe the waiting period from the day he died, or if he divorced. The clear evidence has been established."
"19272","(19272) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: A woman observes the waiting period from the day he dies, or he divorces her if she marries her. The clear statement"
"19273","(19273) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab and Al-Shu’bi, who said: When the clear evidence is established The number is from the day he dies, and if she does not rise, then the day the news comes to her."
"19274","(19274) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; Concerning a man who divorces, or dies while he is absent, he said: If a fair woman stands between him, if she observes the waiting period from the day he dies. Otherwise, who The day the news comes to her."
"19275","(19275) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd who said: When the witnesses testify, who will The day he died, meaning in the waiting period."
"19276","(19276) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Releasing a slave is not a divorce."
"19277","(19277) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, who said: This does not constitute a divorce for him."
"19278","(19278) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Permanent divorce."
"19279","(19279) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hawshab, on the authority of al-Hasan, he was asked about a slave who had returned and had a wife, and he said: If he comes Before the waiting period has expired, then she is his wife, and if it comes after the waiting period has expired, then she has divorced him."
"19280","(19280) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar that if he divorced, he would Al-Raja'i did not enter until he asked for permission, and Al-Sha'bi said: Our companions used to say: He puts on his shoes."
"19281","(19281) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar that he divorced his wife. One divorce, or two divorces, and he used to ask her for permission."
"19282","(19282) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A divorced woman must observe the waiting period in her husband’s house and do not use kohl. He shall wear beautiful eyeliner, and he shall not enter upon her except with her permission, nor shall he be with her in her house."
"19283","(19283) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: If he enters her, let him be quiet. And let him clear his throat and not deceive her by entering."
"19284","(19284) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: If he divorces her once, He is asking her for permission."
"19285","(19285) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Mujahid. They said: He feels By sighing."
"19286","(19286) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He makes her feel the throat."
"19287","(19287) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, he was asked about a man who divorced his wife completely. Does he ask her permission? He said: He sounds and clears his throat. He said: Ibn Abbas said: It is not appropriate for him to see her hair."
"19288","(19288) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar that he used to say: If A man divorced his wife once, or twice, and she did not leave his house except with his permission."
"19289","(19289) Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyya told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, regarding his saying: {No You expel them from their homes, but they will not go out}"
"19290","(19290) Muhammad bin Fudail told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who divorces his wife, the king of the Raj’a said: She should apply kohl and wear dyed hair and see her condition, but she should not ablution. Her clothes"
"19291","(19291) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim; If a man divorces his wife once and for all, the king will take her back. She will beautify herself for him, be exposed to him, and will be concealed."
"19292","(19292) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man divorces his wife twice, or If you divorce him twice, then she is beautifying herself and showing off to him without putting on her veil with him."
"19293","(19293) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, who said: If a man divorces his wife twice, So he asks her permission, and she can wear whatever clothes and jewelry she wants, even if they only have one house. Let them put a screen between them, and greet them when they enter."
"19294","(19294) Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri and his followers, who said about a man who divorces his wife once she divorces him, or Two divorces and they said: You will see for him."
"19295","(19295) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, who said: Ali said: Let you see him, and Ibn Abbas: It is not permissible for him to see her hair."
"19296","(19296) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ata’, who said: She beautifies herself for him and gives herself to him if he divorces her once."
"19297","(19297) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: Ata al-Khurasani wrote to me that he asked Sa`id ibn Al-Musayyab, the jurist of the people of Medina, said: And I think he said: And Sulaiman bin Yasar, on the authority of the divorced woman and the deceased, They said: You should use kohl, dyeing, applying perfume, and combing."
"19298","(19298) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The divorced woman has three And the deceased is equal in adornment."
"19299","(19299) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A woman who has been divorced three times should not apply kohl to herself with cosmetic kohl."
"19300","(19300) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The woman who was divorced on three occasions and the one who died from her. Do not use kohl or dye your hair."
"19301","(19301) Gandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the ruling regarding a divorced woman. Three things: Do not use kohl and do not adorn yourself, and this is more severe. He has someone who died with him."
"19302","(19302) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ata’ al-Khurasani, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The divorced woman has three And the deceased is equal in adornment."
"19303","(19303) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Hafsa Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Umm Atiyya that she said She should not apply kohl or dye her hair, or wear dyed clothing, except a loose garment, and she should not apply perfume except when she has washed herself from her menstrual period. With the word \qast\"" and \""afsafir\"""," it says: in the name of the deceased."""
"19304","(19304) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: He used to forbid it. The deceased, on the authority of perfume and adornment."
"19305","(19305) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayyub ibn Musa, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Safiyyah Uyaynah complained when he died. Ibn Omar, and she used to drip patience within her."
"19306","(19306) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Lahiq bin Humaid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The deceased leaves behind her kohl, perfume, jewelry, and dyes."
"19307","(19307) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Saleh, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, similar to him."
"19308","(19308) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The woman whose husband died does not use kohl. She shall not dye her hair, nor wear any clothing except the garment of a sergeant, and she shall not appear from her house, but she shall visit the fire during the day."
"19309","(19309) Abd al-Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, that Amina bint Uthman’s husband died and she died. We appointed her, so she sent to Aisha to ask her, but she ordered her to use anticonvulsant kohl, so she sent to her, “Indeed, I was My eye came back to her, and I feared for her, so I sent to her. Do not use anti-corrosive kohl, even if your eyes are swollen."
"19310","(19310) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I asked a woman and she said: I am a perfumer’s wife. My husband died, so he forbade her and said: Do not use kohl unless it is necessary."
"19311","(19311) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Badil ibn Misra, on the authority of al-Hasan ibn Muslim ibn Yannaq, On the authority of Safiyya Ibn Shaybah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: The deceased should not wear jewelry during her waiting period."
"19312","(19312) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Ata`, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir said: We do not spend on her, he spends on her from her share."
"19313","(19313) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab and Jabir bin Abdullah, And Al-Hasan said: They used to say: She has no maintenance, the inheritance is sufficient for her."
"19314","(19314) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: From her share.\n(19314 AD) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: From her share."
"19315","(19315) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Qubaisa bin Dhu’ayb said: If you spend on her from Other than her share, she spent on her from the share of what was in her belly."
"19316","(19316) Hushaym and Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He will spend on her from her share."
"19317","(19317) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, that Ibn Abbas said: Concerning the deceased. She is pregnant and we do not support her, and Ibn al-Zubayr judged for us."
"19318","(19318) Waki` told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, about the ruling. He said: It is spent on her from her share, and I heard Waki` say Sufyan used to say: He spends on her from her share."
"19319","(19319) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: I spent on her from her share."
"19320","(19320) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali, Abdullah and Shurayh. They said: It is spent. Ali from all the wealth."
"19321","(19321) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Abdullah and Shurayh, who said: He spends on her from all Money"
"19322","(19322) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Husayn, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: It is spent Ali from all the wealth."
"19323","(19323) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi and Ibrahim, who said: All the money."
"19324","(19324) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: All the money will be spent on her."
"19325","(19325) Waki` told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of al-Hikam, on the authority of Shurayh who said: All the money will be spent on her."
"19326","(19326) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Ibn Ash’u’, who said: He was the judge and judge of the people of Kufa. They say: All the money is spent on her."
"19327","(19327) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Our companions used to say: If the money He spent all the money on her."
"19328","(19328) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The companions of Abdullah They say about a woman whose husband has died: If the money is a lot, then I will spend on it from the boy’s share, and if the money is A little, of all the money."
"19329","(19329) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his leaders and Hammad, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim. They said: The pregnant woman: the deceased. All the money is spent on her."
"19330","(19330) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Yunus, that Ibn Sirin said: He used to provide for every pregnant woman, and he said: Fuli. The mother of the son of Ali bin Khalid, and he thought he should provide for her, so he decided to provide for her without the judge, so he sent for Abd al-Malik bin Ali, so he prevented her. He said: Al-Hasan used to say: He will spend on her, so if she gives birth to him alive, then I will spend on her from the share of her children. If she gives birth to him dead, that will be cancelled."
"19331","(19331) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: If she is the mother of a child, then her master dies on her behalf. So we spent on it from the share of what is in her belly."
"19332","(19332) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Abdullah said: He counted the menstruating divorced woman. And if it is long, Hafs said: Then he mentioned the Sunnah and repeated it."
"19333","(19333) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, and on the authority of Ubaydah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that they said: She should observe the waiting period. With menstruation."
"19334","(19334) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Omar said: If she is divorced The woman had her menstrual period, or two menstrual periods, then she stopped her menstruation. She waited for three months for menstruation, then The waiting period for pregnancy is nine months, then it is permissible for men."
"19335","(19335) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the case of a woman, if he divorced her and she had her menstrual period, or two menstrual periods, she would wait for a year, then after the period she would remain for three months. Then he got married."
"19336","(19336) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja`far, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib, who said: He wrote to me. Al-Zuhri: A man divorced his wife while she was breastfeeding his son, and she remained for seven or eight months without menstruating. It was said to him: If I die, I will inherit from you. He said: Carry me to Othman, so they carried him. Othman sent for Ali and Zaid and asked them, and they said: We see. To inherit it. He said: Why? They said: Because she is not among those who have given up menstruation, nor is she among those who have not menstruated, but breastfeeding prevents her from menstruation. So the man took his son, and when she lost him, she had one menstrual period, then she had another menstrual period in the second month, then he died before he could. The third woman menstruated and inherited it."
"19337","(19337) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar that Al-Ahwas was a man from the people of the Levant. He divorced his wife once, or twice, and he died while bleeding during the third menstrual period, so that matter was reported to his wife. So he asked Fadalah bin Ubaid and those of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about her, but he was not found with them about her. He knew, so he sent a rider on it to Zayd bin Thabit, and he said: She will not inherit it, and if she dies, he will not inherit it. He said: Ibn Umar was seeing That"
"19338","(19338) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah that he divorced his wife once, or Two divorces and she had her menstrual cycle, or she had her menstrual cycle in sixteen or seventeen months, then she did not menstruate The third: Until she died, he came to Abdullah and mentioned that to him, and Abdullah said: May God withhold her inheritance from you and inherit it from her."
"19339","(19339) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, that his grandfather Hibban bin Savior: There were two wives with him, a woman from Banu Hashim and a woman from the Ansar, and he divorced the Ansar and she breastfed him. And if she breastfed, she would remain for a year without menstruating, but Hibban died at the beginning of the year, so Uthman inherited her and said to the Hashemites: This is the opinion of your cousin Ali bin Abi Talib."
"19340","(19340) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, regarding a woman who does not menstruate except during the months. He said: She should observe the menstrual period. Even if you go too far."
"19341","(19341) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, that a man divorced his wife and accused her of Two men in secret and said: Keep quiet about me, so they kept secret about him, until the number of days was over, then they went up to Ali and accused the two witnesses. He flogged them and did not allow him to return to her."
"19342","(19342) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar that Ibn al-Zubayr divorced his wife. He did not teach her anything, so Ibn Umar said: What a miserable thing he did."
"19343","(19343) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, that Shurayh divorced his wife. So they concealed the divorce until her waiting period had ended, and they blamed him for that."
"19344","(19344) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, who said: Ali said: The two arbiters are combined. God and them He separates."
"19345","(19345) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, who said: What the two arbiters have decided is permissible."
"19346","(19346) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama, who said: The two arbiters can unite them, if they will, and separate them, if they will."
"19347","(19347) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Mujahid, regarding the Almighty’s saying: {If they desire reform, He will succeed. God is between them} He said: They are the two arbitrators."
"19348","(19348) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of al-hukm. He said: If the two arbitrators disagree, then no: he shall rule for them and make Someone else, and if they agree, their ruling is permissible."
"19349","(19349) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus regarding the two arbitrators: If they give a ruling, then take their ruling and do not follow a trace. Other than them, even if they had already ruled against you before them."
"19350","(19350) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: “They want reform.” May God grant success between them. He said: They are the two arbitrators."
"19351","(19351) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, who said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab about a man who is incapable. About his maintenance with his wife, and he said: He should separate them, so I said: Sunnah? He said: Sunnah."
"19352","(19352) Ali bin Musahir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab. He said: I asked him about the man. He is unable to provide for his wife, so he said: He must provide, or he will be divorced."
"19353","(19353) Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: He should be kept well with him. He said: It has informed me that Omar ibn Abd Al-Aziz said that."
"19354","(19354) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man is unable to support his wife, he should not separate them."
"19355","(19355) Omar bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who is unable to provide for his wife. He said: There should be no separation between them. A woman is afflicted, so let her be patient."
"19356","(19356) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, who said: I asked Hammad about a man who married a woman and did not have anything to spend on. He said: It will be postponed for a year. I said: If not? He said: He will divorce her."
"19357","(19357) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: It is different. Between them."
"19358","(19358) Abdullah bin Numayr told us: Ubaid Allah bin Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Omar wrote to the commanders of the soldiers. As for one of the people of Medina who was absent from his wives, he ordered them to return to their wives, either to separate from each other, or to They will be sent to spend, so whoever of them separates from them, let him be sent to spend what he left behind."
"19359","(19359) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Makin, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote: He who is absent from his wife. Two years, then let him divorce her, or let him remain close to her."
"19360","(19360) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Makin, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Whoever is absent from his wife for two years should divorce him. Or to close to her."
"19361","(19361) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: If a man is absent for a long period of time, he should spend on his wife’s behalf. His wife, or he divorced her."
"19362","(19362) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam; He did not see any need to pay for someone who was absent."
"19363","(19363) Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If a man is absent from his wife for a long period of time, he should send To provide maintenance to her, or to divorce her."
"19364","(19364) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who marries a woman, he said: He will not spend on her until he has consummated the sexual intercourse with her."
"19365","(19365) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Kamil bin Fudail, who said: I asked Al-Sha’bi about a man who married a woman and he did not He entered with her, then he disappeared from her, and when he came, she made him pay for her, so Al-Sha’bi said: He will not spend with her until he enters with her."
"19366","(19366) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, saying: Yunus was asked about a man who married a woman, then disappeared from her before he He enters with her, does she have any maintenance? He said: Al-Hassan did not see that he was obligated to spend on her until he entered with her unless they told him: Take her, and he did not take her."
"19367","(19367) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Hussam ibn Misk, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The woman has no right to Her husband supports you except from the day she asks for that."
"19368","(19368) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amir, who said: It is not permissible for a man to spend on his wife if she is in prison. From her."
"19369","(19369) Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that he was asked about a woman who went out of She is disobedient to her husband. Does she have to spend on her? He said: No, even if she stays for twenty years."
"19370","(19370) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, who said: I asked the ruling about a woman who left her husband’s house in disobedience. No expense? He said: Yes. I asked Hammad and he said: She has no means of spending."
"19371","(19371) Baz bin Asad narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Harun, who said: I asked Al-Hasan about a woman who came out in conflict. For her husband, does she have any maintenance? He said: It has walls of dirt."
"19372","(19372) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Salih that Uthman inherited the wife of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf. When he divorced her during his illness after the end of the waiting period."
"19373","(19373) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of a man from Quraysh, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, who said: If he divorced her If he is sick, I inherit from him, even if a year has passed, unless he recovers, or she marries him."
"19374","(19374) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaiki, who said: I asked Ibn al-Zubayr about A man divorced his wife while he was sick, then he died, and he said: His son Othman inherited Al-Asbagh Al-Kalbiyya, but as for me, I do not see it. To inherit your property."
"19375","(19375) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr, that Khaled bin Abdullah asked Al-Hasan about a man who divorced He took his wife for three days during his illness, then he died, and her waiting period had ended. He said: She shall inherit."
"19376","(19376) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he fell ill for a year, I would inherit from him."
"19377","(19377) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: Urwa came to me. Al-Bariqi from Omar; Concerning a man who divorces his wife three times during her illness: she shall inherit from her as long as she is within the waiting period, but he shall not inherit from her."
"19378","(19378) Abu Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: She inherits it and he does not inherit it as long as it lasts. The number"
"19379","(19379) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father, that Al-Hasan bin Ali divorced his wife while he was ill, and he died. So I inherited it."
"19380","(19380) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud and Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: If he divorces three times during his illness I inherited it as long as it was within the waiting period."
"19381","(19381) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, that the mother of the sons, the daughter of Uyaynah bin Hisn, was under Othman bin Affan, when he was besieged, he divorced her, and he had sent to her to buy her money from her, but she refused, so when he was killed, she came to Ali. So she mentioned that to him, and he said: He left her until, when he was about to die, he divorced her, so he inherited her."
"19382","(19382) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, that Hisham bin Hubaira wrote to Shurayh He asked him about a man who divorced his wife three times during his illness, and Sharih wrote to him: He is a fugitive from the Book of God. inheritance"
"19383","(19383) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos; Concerning a man who divorced his wife three times during her illness, he said: She shall inherit from him as long as she is within the waiting period."
"19384","(19384) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, who said: I asked Urwa about a man who divorces his wife outright. Should I inherit? One the other? Does she have any means of spending? He said: Neither of them inherits from the other, nor does he spend on her unless she is pregnant, in which case he spends on her until she gives birth, or he divorces her. During his illness"
"19385","(19385) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Sa`id bin Abi Aroub told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Aisha that she said regarding a woman who has been divorced three times while he is ill: She shall inherit him as long as she is within the waiting period."
"19386","(19386) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: They used to say: You do not disagree with someone who fled from The Book of God was returned to him, meaning; Concerning a man who divorces his wife while he is sick."
"19387","(19387) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith, about a man who was under a divorce from a woman, and he had He divorced her twice before that, so he divorced her during his illness and he died during the waiting period: he neither inherits from her nor she inherits from her."
"19388","(19388) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Yunus, who said: Al-Hasan used to say: If a man said: If I enter the house of so-and-so’s children So he divorced your wife, and he forgot and entered her, or he entered her without knowing it. He said: He would make it like an intentional one, except that He stipulates that he says: Unless I forget you."
"19389","(19389) Yahya bin Sulaym told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Othman, who said: My brother Omar bin Othman swore that he would free his female slave. He told him not to drink from her hand, until he hit him for the time, but he forgot before the time had passed and drank, so she asked him for a fatwa, he was generous and diligent. And Saeed bin Jubair, and Ali Al-Azdi, all of them thought that she was free."
"19390","(19390) Yahya bin Sulaym narrated to us, saying: This hadith was narrated to us by Ibn Juraij, who denied that he was a giver. He sees something in forgetfulness. He said, and Ataa said: I have been informed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God has transcended his nation. About three things: about mistakes, forgetfulness, and what they were forced to do. (Hakim 362)"
"19391","(19391) I narrated on the authority of Ibn Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri (h), on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Omar Ibn Abd al-Aziz, that they were required to divorce due to forgetfulness."
"19392","(19392) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Abdul Karim Abi Umayyah, on the authority of the companions of Abdullah bin Masoud that It is permissible for him."
"19393","(19393) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He was asked about a man who said to another: You are envious, and he said: The other: We envy his wife, who has been divorced three times. He said: Yes. He said: You have both been disappointed and lost, and your wife has estranged you from both of you."
"19394","(19394) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith, who said: I condemn them and command them to fear God, and I say: You know best. By what you both swore to him. He said: And the chapter on religiosity is in this and the like."
"19395","(19395) Abdul-Ala told us, saying: Saeed was asked about two men, one of whom said to a bird: If it is not a crow, then his wife. He divorced three times, and the other said: If it is not a pigeon, then his wife is divorced three times. He told us about his followers, who said: If the bird flies and you do not know it. Whatever it is, neither this is close to it nor is this close to it."
"19396","(19396) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Bashir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, about two men whom a bird passed by, and one of them said: His wife is divorced if he is not a bird, and the other said: His wife is divorced if he is not a crow, and the bird flew away and said: They will separate each other. Their wives"
"19397","(19397) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, who said: Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hamza bin Abdullah bin Omar said: She was married to Ibn Omar, and he admired her, and Omar disliked her, so he said to him: They divorced her, but she refused, so Omar mentioned her to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Obey your father. And he divorced her. (Tirmidhi 1189 and Abu Dawud 5095)"
"19398","(19398) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of Abu Talha Al-Asadi, who said: I was sitting with Ibn Abbas, and he came to him. Two Bedouins were separated from him, and one of them said: I was looking for my own camels, so I stayed with a people, and their girl pleased me. So I married her, and my parents swore that they would never have sexual intercourse with her, and the boy swore and said: He owes a thousand freed, a thousand freed, and a thousand freed. If he divorces her, then Ibn Abbas said: I am not the one commanding you to divorce your wife or to free your parents. He said: So what should I do? With this woman? He said: Justify your parents."
"19399","(19399) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, who said: He was from the neighborhood, a young man in A house that his mother continued until she married him to her cousin, and he was suspended from her, then his mother said to him: Divorce her, and he said: I cannot. She became attached to something that I cannot divorce her with. She said: Your food and drink are forbidden to me until you divorce her. So he left. To Abu Darda' to the Levant, and he mentioned his situation to him, and he said: I am not the one who commanded you to divorce your wife, nor am I the one who commanded you. To disobey your mother."
"19400","(19400) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A man came to him and said: His mother ordered him to get married, then After that, she ordered him to divorce him, and Al-Hasan said: Divorcing his wife is not honoring his mother in anything."
"19401","(19401) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Amr ibn Haram, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zaid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Concerning a man who had wives and divorced one of them, then he died, not knowing which of them he divorced? He said: Ibn Abbas said: They will get from divorce what they get from inheritance."
"19402","(19402) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, about a man who had four wives and he divorced. One of them, then he married another, then he died and did not know which of them he divorced. He said: Al-Sha’abi said: For the first four there are three quarters. Inheritance and a quarter for the fifth."
"19403","(19403) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, about a man who had four He divorced one of them without knowing which of them he divorced? Then he married a fifth, then he died. He said: A quarter of the inheritance is completed for this woman whom he married and what remained between them. The four"
"19404","(19404) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, about a man who had four wives, and he divorced one of them, then He married a fifth, then died without knowing which of them he divorced? He said: A quarter of an eighth for the one he recently married, and three-quarters for those four."
"19405","(19405) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: Ata’ was asked about that and he said: A quarter of a quarter, or a quarter of an eighth. To the one he later married and divided what remained between them."
"19406","(19406) Abdul Wahhab bin Ata’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and Al-Hasan. They said: He knocks between us"
"19407","(19407) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Bishr bin Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who said to his wife: He is divorced unless he marries her. He said: He is his wife until he marries, but if he dies One of them, so there is no inheritance between them."
"19408","(19408) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, regarding a man who swore: “His wife is divorced unless he beats her.” He gave his boy a hundred lashes. He said: This is his wife until the boy dies."
"19409","(19409) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ghaylan, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: His wife is divorced unless he beats his servant. So he stayed, and said: He will have intercourse with her and they will go together."
"19410","(19410) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, regarding a man who said: If I do not gain sight, then his wife will be divorced. He said: So he did not He came to her until she died, then he came to her after that, saying: He has no inheritance from her, but his oaths have become clear now."
"19411","(19411) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: If he gains sight after death, he inherits it."
"19412","(19412) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and Al-Hasan. They said: Concerning a man who says to his wife: If I do not marry her, and if I do not take you out, then you are divorced. They said: He should not approach her, even if He died before that and they did not inherit anything from each other."
"19413","(19413) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who said: If I do not go out to a mediator, then his wife will be divorced. He said: He will cheat on her and they will not inherit inheritance, and Ibn Sirin said: No. He cheated on her until he did what he said."
"19414","(19414) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Shurayh said: Urwa al-Bariqi came to me from Omar in A man who is divorced three times during his illness: She inherits from her as long as she is within the waiting period. He does not inherit from her, but the waiting period for her husband is due."
"19415","(19415) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: She must have the ‘iddah of her husband who died."
"19416","(19416) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, who said: If a man dies during her waiting period, she must wait for him. Her husband died after four months and ten days."
"19417","(19417) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A serious matter of divorce: If she inherits, she must observe the waiting period."
"19418","(19418) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah that he said: If nothing remains of her waiting period except One day, then he died, and she inherited it and continued the number of the deceased."
"19419","(19419) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: The counting of days resumes."
"19420","(19420) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was forbidden. The mother of his children and swore that he would not approach her, so God Almighty revealed: {O Prophet, why have you forbidden what God has made lawful for you, seeking to please You? Your wives} until the end of the verse, and it was said to him: As for what is forbidden, it is permissible, and as for the oath that you swore to her, God has made it lawful for you. Your oaths are in the oath that you swore to. (Nasa’i 8907, Ibn Jarir 156)"
"19421","(19421) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who said to the mother of his children: You are forbidden to me. He said: He will make amends for his oath and come to his female slaves."
"19422","(19422) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, who said: If he says: I will kill him. It is forbidden for him. He said: He will expiate his oath and come to his nation."
"19423","(19423) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Ata’ Al-Khurasani, that a man divorced his wife and three people witnessed him. Every man who testifies in a place other than that of his companion, so Abdullah bin Mawhib decided that she should divorce him."
"19424","(19424) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: If a man says to his wife: You are divorced if you enter so-and-so’s house, Then she entered a part of her body, and the divorce occurred upon her."
"19425","(19425) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, about a man who said to his wife: Do not be permissible for me. He said: His intention is if he intends. One, then one, and if he intends three, then three."
"19426","(19426) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, the same."
"19427","(19427) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Waqid, a client of Banu Hanzali, who said: Ata bin Abi Rabah was asked about a man. He took a thief and the people gathered against him and asked him to leave him, so he said: If you leave him, then his wife will be divorced three times, so he prevailed upon him. He escaped from him. He said: Then Ata’ said: There is nothing wrong with him, but he defeated himself."
"19428","(19428) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he used to say: If a man marries his daughter while she is young So he decided to take her off, as that was permissible for her. Yunus said: He was not good and did not think so."
"19429","(19429) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Shurayh that a man divorced her daughter and she did not consent. He said: The divorce took place on her. Her father is a guarantor of what he ransomed for."
"19430","(19430) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, and the ruling regarding a woman, he said to her Her husband: If she menstruates, then you are divorced, and her menstruation stops and she becomes pregnant. They said: He will have intercourse with her until she menstruates, and Amer said: If he reconciles. The near, it is good in the far away."
"19431","(19431) Waki’ told us: Shu’abi told us: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who said to his wife: You are divorced whenever Whatever you wish, the arbiter said: Whenever she wishes, she is divorced, and Hammad said: Marwa."
"19432","(19432) Affan narrated to us, saying: Abu Awani narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If the father marries, then the divorce is in the father’s hands. Mujahid said: Whoever has the power to marry, then in his power is divorce."
"19433","(19433) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, that he thought it was permissible."
"19434","(19434) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that they were of the opinion that a polytheistic divorce permissible"
"19435","(19435) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he did not consider it permissible."
"19436","(19436) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: I said to Ata’: I have informed you that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left Did the people of the pre-Islamic era adhere to their customs of marriage or divorce? He said: Yes."
"19437","(19437) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, who said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad, and they said: It is permissible, meaning a polytheistic divorce."
"19438","(19438) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Amir, who said: Islam did not increase him except in hardship."
"19439","(19439) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, that a man divorced his wife in the pre-Islamic era. She was divorced twice, then he converted to Islam and he divorced her once in Islam, so Omar asked Abd al-Rahman bin Awf and he said: His divorce was due to polytheism. Nothing."
"19440","(19440) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha’i, on the authority of Ikrimah, in the Almighty’s saying: {And it is not lawful for them. To conceal what God created in their wombs. He said: menstruation, then Khaled said: blood."
"19441","(19441) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid and Ibrahim. One of them said: The rope, And menstruation, and the other said: menstruation."
"19442","(19442) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: To say: I am pregnant, and not Pregnant, or she says: I am pregnant, but she is not pregnant."
"19443","(19443) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibn Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas He said: menstruation and pregnancy, and Abraham said: pregnancy."
"19444","(19444) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Childbirth and menstruation."
"19445","(19445) Shababah told us, on the authority of Warqa’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: {And it is not permissible for them to conceal What God has created in our wombs} He said: It is not permissible for a divorced woman to say: I am menstruating, and she is not menstruating, nor to say: I am pregnant. She is not pregnant and does not say: I am not pregnant, but she is pregnant."
"19446","(19446) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah (And it is not lawful for them to conceal what God has created In their wombs) He said: menstruation."
"19447","(19447) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid: “And it is not lawful for them to conceal what He has created.” God is in our wombs. He said: Pregnancy and menstruation. He said: And Abraham said: Menstruation alone."
"19448","(19448) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Saad ibn Ibrahim, that a man said to his wife: You are divorced. Al-Qasim and Salim asked, and they said: We think that we should swear to him absolutely what he wanted."
"19449","(19449) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Lahia, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Abi Ja`far, on the authority of Bukair ibn Abd. Allah ibn al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of a man who said to his wife: You are divorced, and he did not name the number of divorces. He said: We carry that for him, if One, two, or three niyyah."
"19450","(19450) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: We give to a divorced woman every day half a saa’ of wheat."
"19451","(19451) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, about a woman whose husband had harmed her, and then Al-Shu’bi imposed on her. Every month there are fifteen saa's of wheat and two dirhams."
"19452","(19452) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Minhal bin Khalifa, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of It is required that twelve dirhams be paid to a woman and her servant every month: four for the servant and eight for the woman."
"19453","(19453) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Umm Khasib Al-Wabashiyah, that her husband died and left her pregnant, so she disputed with her. Sharih, so he decided that fifteen percent of the total money should be spent on her."
"19454","(19454) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: He spends on one servant."
"19455","(19455) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Omar disputed with Umm Asim about Asim to Abu Bakr. So he decided for her as long as he did not grow up, or get married and choose for himself. He said: She is the kindest, the most gentle, the gentlest, and the most compassionate. And have mercy."
"19456","(19456) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Ismail bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Ghanam said: I witnessed Omar give a boy the choice between his father and his mother."
"19457","(19457) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub and Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh who said: The father is more right, and the mother is more gentle."
"19458","(19458) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Saad, or it was narrated on his authority, on the authority of Hilal bin Abi Maimunah, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Huraira, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave a boy the choice between his two parents. (Tirmidhi 1357. Ahmad 2/246)"
"19459","(19459) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: She has more right to her children, even if she marries."
"19460","(19460) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man divorces his wife, he has more right. With her children unless she gets married or leaves the earth with them."
"19461","(19461) Abdullah told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq that he gave a boy the choice between his parents. Which one does he choose?"
"19462","(19462) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Salman Abi Maimouna, on the authority of Abi Hariri said: A woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, whose husband had divorced her, and she wanted to take She has two sons. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: They were curious about it, and the man said: Who will come between me and my son? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the son: Choose whichever you want. He said: So he chose his mother, and she went with him.\n(Ahmad 2/447, Tahawi 3088)"
"19463","(19463) Hafs told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that Abu Bakr judged Asim ibn Omar for his mother, and he judged Omar. By spending"
"19464","(19464) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id ibn Abi Aroub narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, that Omar Ibn Al-Khattab divorced Umm Asim, then he went to her, and Asim was in her lap. He wanted to take her from her, so they quarreled. Between them until the boy cried, so they went to Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr said to him: O Omar, wipe her and quarantine her. And its fragrance is better for him than yours, until the boy grows old and chooses it."
"19465","(19465) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Al-Qasim, that Omar ibn Al-Khattab divorced his wife Jamila bint Asim ibn Thabit Ibn Abi Al-Aqlah, so she got married, then Omar came and took his son, and the suns overtook him. His son, Abi Amer Al-Ansariyy, and he Umm Jamila, so she took him, so they approached Abu Bakr while they were holding each other together, so he said to Omar: Leave between her and her son. So I took it."
"19466","(19466) Waki` bin al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka`b, that a woman from the family Al-Badia was with a man from her paternal uncles, and he died, so a man from the Ansar married her, and the maid’s paternal cousins came to her. They said: They took our daughter. She said: I implore you, by God, to separate me from my daughter, for I am pregnant and I am breastfeeding, and not One last occasion because my daughter was close to me but they refused. She said: Your appointment is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then he said: If the Messenger of God gives you a choice. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then you said: I choose God and faith and the home of the immigrants and the Ansar. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, you shall not take it away as long as my neck remains in its place. And they came to Abu Bakr and he decided for them. With her, Bilal said: O successor of the Messenger of God, this group was present and this woman was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. They disputed and decided about her to her mother, so Abu Bakr said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, they will not go with her as long as she lasts. He was hanged in her place, and he gave her to her mother."
"19467","(19467) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Zakariya, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, about a slave girl whose mother wanted to take her out. From Kufa, and he said: Her intercourse is more deserving of her than her mother if she goes out."
"19468","(19468) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abdullah bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Amara bin Rabi’ah Al-Jarmiy. He said: My father fought towards the sea in some of those battles. He said: He was killed, so my uncle came to take me, so my mother argued with him to Ali said: And with me is a younger brother of mine who said: So Ali gave me three choices, so I chose my mother, but my uncle refused to accept. He said: Then Ali poked him with his hand and hit him with his fist and said: This is also the case if he had reached the age of 10. He would have been better."
"19469","(19469) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, who said: Shuraih was given the choice of an orphan boy and a slave girl, so the slave girl chose Her master, and the boy chose his paternal aunt according to what he thought best, and Shurayh allowed him to do so."
"19470","(19470) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi regarding breastfeeding The boy said: His mother has more right to him than she was in Egypt, so if she wants to go out with him to the black, then the saints."
"19471","(19471) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, who said: I heard him say: I said to Ibrahim: What Al-Ilaa? He said: To swear: He will not speak to her, nor will he have intercourse with her, nor will he put his head and hers together, nor will he provoke her to anger, or It is the worst of it."
"19472","(19472) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, about a man who said to his wife: By God As for Aswank, he said: If what he meant by that was a woman whom he would marry, or a female slave whom he would entertain, then it is nothing, even if He meant intercourse, so it is sexual intercourse."
"19473","(19473) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, he said: I heard Al-Hakam saying: Concerning a man who said to his wife: “By God, I will make you worse.” So he left her for four months. He said: “So it is a betrayal.”"
"19474","(19474) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that a man claimed the belongings of the house, so they came. Four women went to Shurayh and they testified. They said: We gave him the dowry and we said: He prepared it, so he prepared it and paid for it with the goods. And he said: Her barrenness is from your owner."
"19475","(19475) Abd al-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: I wrote to Abu Qalabi asking him about the man who spoke: The House Concerning a woman’s belongings, who are they for? He said: He has what he did not give her."
"19476","(19476) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: What is for men is for men, and what is for women is for For the women, and whatever remains is for the one who established the clear proof."
"19477","(19477) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whatever is for men is for men, and whatever is for women is For women, and what remains between them."
"19478","(19478) Abd bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the woman whose husband died, he said: She has not kept her wealth except what was of the poor man’s belongings. And the shirt and the like."
"19479","(19479) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, that he was asked about household items, and he said: Women’s clothing is for the woman. A man's clothing is for the man, and whenever they quarrel and it is not about this person, it is the one in his hand."
"19480","(19480) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that he heard him say: If a woman enters upon Her husband and she has some jewelry and other things, so she stays with her husband until she dies, then it is an inheritance, provided that her family establishes clear evidence. He was naked with her, unless they knew about that husband during her life before her death."
"19481","(19481) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, who said: I heard a sheikh who was more advanced than Shurayh. It is reported on the authority of Shurayh that he said regarding household items: Whatever weapons or belongings of a man belong to the man."
"19482","(19482) Yahya ibn Abi Ghani told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the ruling, he said: If a man dies and leaves behind any property The house, as it belongs to the man, does not belong to the woman, it belongs to the man, and what belongs to the woman does not belong to the man, it For the woman, and what is for men and women is for the man unless the woman upholds the clear statement that it is for her."
"19483","(19483) Hushaym and Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, who said: Breastfeeding a boy from His share"
"19484","(19484) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: His breastfeeding is his share."
"19485","(19485) Ismail Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Abdullah Ibn Utba came to breastfeed a boy. So he put his breastfeeding in his wealth and said to his guardian: If he had no money, we would put his breastfeeding in your wealth. Don’t you see him saying: {And the heir shall do the same}"
"19486","(19486) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He used to say: If Rida’a fulfills his share, then it is From his share, and if it is not fulfilled, then it is from the entire wealth."
"19487","(19487) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Sharih in the infant: He spends Of his share, be it little, or much."
"19488","(19488) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Our companions used to say: If the money All the money was spent on him."
"19489","(19489) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: He used to say: spending. And breastfeeding comes from all wealth."
"19490","(19490) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: {And the heir is responsible for the same} He said: The heir has the same duty as his father, to breastfeed for him."
"19491","(19491) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim {and upon the heir is the same} like His father does not have to breastfeed."
"19492","(19492) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim. They said: The breastfeeding of a boy."
"19493","(19493) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath and Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan: {And the heir is responsible for the same}, and he said: breastfeeding."
"19494","(19494) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He is obligated to breastfeed, but he is not obligated to support the pregnant woman."
"19495","(19495) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: No harm is done."
"19496","(19496) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, in these verses: {And upon the heir is the same} He said: The father dies and leaves behind a young son. If he has money, he can breastfeed him with his money, and if he does not have money, he can breastfeed him. On her nerves."
"19497","(19497) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: They came to an orphanage. Omar, and he said: Spend on him. He said: If I had only found the furthest members of his clan, I would have imposed it on them."
"19498","(19498) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: I witnessed Abdullah bin Utba, who said For the guardian of an orphan: If he had no money, I would have made a payment for you to support him, because God Almighty says: {And upon the heir is the like. That}"
"19499","(19499) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak {and the heir is responsible for that}. He said: He is the father. It means: The maintenance is on the father, and if he does not have it, then it is on the guardian, and if he does not have it, then the mother is forced to breastfeed him. If the child knows her and does not take it from anyone else, she is forced to breastfeed him."
"19500","(19500) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {And upon the heir is the same} He said: The heir must not be harmed."
"19501","(19501) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Al-Dahhak: {And upon the heir Like that} He said: It is not harmed."
"19502","(19502) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab that Omar bin Al-Khattab made a ransom to the cousins of his cousin by breastfeeding him on his cousin. (Ibn Jarir 500)"
"19503","(19503) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan: And upon the heir is like that. He said: upon Men but not women."
"19504","(19504) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He was asked about a boy who has a mother and a paternal uncle, and the mother is well-off and the paternal uncle is He is insolvent, so he said: The maintenance is on the uncle."
"19505","(19505) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit He said: If there is a paternal uncle and a mother, then the mother is responsible according to the amount of her inheritance and the paternal uncle is responsible according to the amount of his inheritance."
"19506","(19506) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: If a man divorces his wife, he leaves her There was a child from him, and he had to breastfeed."
"19507","(19507) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Ali Breastfeed him until you wean him."
"19508","(19508) Abu Bakr al-Hanafi told us, on the authority of al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, who said: I asked al-Qasim ibn Muhammad about a woman’s What is her daughter's money? He said: Yes, I see it as truth."
"19509","(19509) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I said to Ata’: The orphan’s mother is in need. Should I provide for him? Ali of his money? Ataa said: She has nothing? I said: No, he said: Yes."
"19510","(19510) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: They will inherit each other as long as they do not touch each other."
"19511","(19511) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: They will inherit each other as long as they do not touch each other."
"19512","(19512) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If one of them dies before the curse, they inherit inheritance."
"19513","(19513) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, who said: He inherits it, and Al-Hakam said: He will inherit it. And he inherits it."
"19514","(19514) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrim, who said about a man who slandered his wife and she died before He cursed her and said: If he tells a lie about himself, he will be flogged and inherits, but if he appoints witnesses, he will inherit, and if he swears, he will not inherit."
"19515","(19515) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zaid that he said: If one of them dies before... The cursed woman, if she acknowledges them, she will be stoned and the inheritance goes to her. If she is stubborn, she inherits, but if she does not acknowledge one of them. There is no inheritance for her and no covenant with her."
"19516","(19516) Ismail bin Aliyah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, about a man who slandered his wife, then she died. They said: He shall inherit from her. Nor shall we curse them between them."
"19517","(19517) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He will be flogged and not cursed after death."
"19518","(19518) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: If he slandered her, then she died before he cursed her, he said: If he wishes, he can deny himself and inherit, and if he wishes, he may curse himself and not inherit."
"19519","(19519) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They will inherit each other as long as they do not touch each other."
"19520","(19520) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, regarding a woman who died while pregnant, saying: She is supported by All the money until you deposit it, then the inheritance is divided."
"19521","(19521) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man dies and his wife is pregnant, the inheritance is not divided. Until you are humbled"
"19522","(19522) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Ad-Dahhak, who said: The share of a male is divided and left. If it is a female, it is returned to the heirs, and if it is a male, it is his."
"19523","(19523) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hammad, who said: Every person will be forced to A mahram who must spend on his mahram."
"19524","(19524) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Every heir is obligated to provide for himself."
"19525","(19525) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan that Omar forced a man to provide for his nephew."
"19526","(19526) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: A man is forced to support his parents and spend on them. With kindness."
"19527","(19527) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He is forced to support his brother. If he is insolvent."
"19528","(19528) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, saying: Ash’ath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he was obligated to give birth to his son if he was poor. The grandfather was rich."
"19529","(19529) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, a man said to Jabir ibn Zayd: My father deprives me of his wealth, so he says: No. He spent something on you, and he said: Take from your father’s money in a reasonable manner."
"19530","(19530) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who says to his wife: O brother. He said: This and two dates are only one."
"19531","(19531) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Amr ibn Shuaib, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard A man says to his wife, “O my brother.” He said: Do not say to her: “O my brother.” (Abu Dawud 2203)"
"19532","(19532) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ziyad al-Alam, on the authority of al-Hasan; Concerning a woman who absented a man from your deed and he said: You are divorced three times if you have not absent her. Al-Hasan said: If he is truthful Here is his wife, and I heard Hammad saying: He will pay debts in this regard."
"19533","(19533) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, about a man whose wife claimed that he had divorced her. So she took him to the Sultan, and he made him swear that he had not divorced him. Then she had him returned to him and he died. Al-Hasan said: She shall inherit him."
"19534","(19534) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that he was asked about a man who divorced his wife with two men. And a woman, and one of the two men and the woman witnessed, but the other was absent. He said: She will be isolated from him until the absent person comes."
"19535","(19535) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, and Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man says: He spoke to his brother and he divorced his wife three times, and if he wished he could divorce her once, then leave her until her waiting period is over. She spoke to his brother, then he married her if he wanted later."
"19536","(19536) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, who said: A man married a woman according to a covenant. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, divorced her. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Did I divorce her? He said: Yes, he said: Is there any harm? He said: No, Messenger of God. Then he married another woman, then divorced her. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Did I divorce her? He said: Yes, he said: Is there any harm? He said: No, Messenger of God. Then he married another woman, then divorced her. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Did you divorce her? He said: Yes, he said: Is there any harm? He said: No, Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the third day: Indeed, God does not love Every taster is a man, but not every taster is a woman.\n(Daraqutni 5167, Bazar 1498)"
"19537","(19537) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Ma`rif, on the authority of Muharib ibn Dathar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is nothing that God has made lawful that he hates more than divorce. (Abu Daou 2170)"
"19538","(19538) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: Ali said: O people of Iraq, or People of Kufa, do not marry Hasan, for he is a divorced man."
"19539","(19539) Hatim narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of his father, who said: Ali said: Al-Hasan continued to marry and divorce until it was deemed appropriate. To be enmity among the tribes."
"19540","(19540) Abdul-Ala told us, he said: He was asked about a man who said to his wife: If I had not given such-and-such to you, then you He divorced three times. He said: Sa`id told us, on the authority of his leaders, that he said: If she is with him, otherwise she has separated from him."
"19541","(19541) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a woman, her husband said to her: If I do not spend ten dirhams on you every month, then you are divorced three times. She said: The woman: Three months have passed and you have not spent anything on me. He said: The saying is what the man said, except that the woman should establish the clear truth. He did not spend on her."
"19542","(19542) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Kufi, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, about a man who said to his adversary: “If I do not repay you, He met you before sunset and his wife was divorced. He said: He met him the next day and claimed that he had not given him anything. He said: She told him His wife: She has divorced me. He said: So I disputed with him to Al-Shu’bi, and Al-Shu’bi said: As for your wife, we will condemn you over her. As for the man So I made it clear to you that you gave him his money, otherwise he will give him what he deserves."
"19543","(19543) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he said: Concerning a man who says to his wife: “I took you off,” and he did not take her off. He said: “He took her off,” and there is nothing wrong with him."
"19544","(19544) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said: A free woman should not be forced to breastfeed and the mother of the child should not be forced."
"19545","(19545) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: If a woman has a breastfeeding boy, she has more right to him. She has the reward of breastfeeding like her, if she accepts him, and if she does not accept him, then he breastfeeds for her from someone else, if the boy accepts from someone else. So, if he does not accept, she will be forced to breastfeed him and given a similar reward."
"19546","(19546) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr: {And if you agree, another woman will breastfeed him} He said: If breastfeeding is based on something, the mother has more right to it."
"19547","(19547) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: If the child does not take from someone else and there is fear for him, it will be forced upon him."
"19548","(19548) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, who said: Ibn Abbas said: {Except that They have committed a clearly obscene act. He said: An obscene act is to commit indecency against its family. If it does that, it is permissible for them to do so. They take it out."
"19549","(19549) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, in God Almighty said: (Unless they commit an obvious indecency) He said: Her leaving her house is an obvious indecency."
"19550","(1955) Ishaq bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Hammad: {And they will not go out unless they bring an indecent person. Making clear} He said: Unless you go out to a limit."
"19551","(19551) Ibn Abi Ghani narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, in the Almighty’s saying: {Unless they commit an indecency. Clearly, clear indecency, disobedience to the husband."
"19552","(19552) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of a man, on the authority of al-Sha`bi: {Unless they commit clearly obscene acts} He said: Her going out is obscene."
"19553","(19553) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, about a man who took a morsel, and he said: A man: If you do not eat it, then your wife is divorced. Then Sanur passed and took the morsel of food, and he said: Your wife is divorced."
"19554","(19554) Ubaidah bin Humaid told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: A man came to Al-Sha’bi and said: A man said to his wife: If you do not eat this arak, then his wife has been divorced three times, so the felines came and took the arak, and Al-Sha’abi said: He did not make There is no way out, God has not created a way out for it."
"19555","(19555) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I was told by someone who heard Abraham and a man bring him a letter, and he said: A man wrote to his wife, and he put her order in her hand, so she read the letter, then put it under the bed, and she got up and did not say anything. Nothing. He said: Nothing."
"19556","(19556) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: If a slave is divorced, the king of taking him back will have the right to provide for him."
"19557","(19557) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he claims to take him back after the end of the waiting period, then he must do so. The clear statement"
"19558","(19558) Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: If he claims to have returned after the end of his promise, he will not be believed. And if he comes with clear evidence."
"19559","(19559) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: If he said after the end of the count: I saw you and he was not believed."
"19560","(19560) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Zayd ibn Zadi, a client of Bajil, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, that he was asked about a man Two men testified that he divorced his wife, so the judge separated them, so one of the witnesses came back and the other married her. He said: Al-Sha’bi said: The judgment has passed, and no attention is paid to the return of the one who returned."
"19561","(19561) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Sami’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Razin, who said: He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. A man, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: O Messenger of God, have you seen the words of God Almighty: {Divorce is twice, then withholding it on a fair basis or releasing it. With goodness} So where is the third? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: {Containing oneself with kindness or releasing oneself with kindness} The third verse. (Abu Dawud 220, Bayhaqi 340)"
"19562","(19562) Abdullah bin Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: A man said to his wife at the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace: I am not closer to you and you are not better than me. She said: So what do you do? He said: I will divorce you until the end of your waiting period approaches. I will take you back. Then she was frightened, so she went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and God Almighty revealed: {Containing oneself with kindness or releasing oneself with kindness} He said: Then the people received him as a new man, both those who had been divorced and those who had not been divorced. (Tirmidhi 1192, Malik 80)"
"19563","(19563) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simmak, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: {Twice divorce, then withholding it on a fair basis or releasing it. With goodness} He said: If a man wants to divorce his wife, he may divorce her twice. If he wants to take her back, then she He has the right to take her back, and if he wishes, he may divorce her again, then she is not permissible for him until she marries another husband."
"19564","(19564) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, saying: Hassan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, who said: I heard Ikrimah say: {Divorce is twice. So keeping you with kindness or letting go with kindness} He said: If a man divorces one of his women, then if he wishes he may marry her, and if he divorces her Two women, and if he wishes, he may marry her. If he divorces her three times, then she is not permissible for him until she marries another husband."
"19565","(19565) Shababah told us, on the authority of Warqa’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: {Twice divorce, then withholding on a reasonable basis or... Dismissal with goodness} He said: A man divorces his wife in a state of ritual purity, without intercourse. If she menstruates, then becomes pure, then the recitation has been completed. Then he divorced the second woman just as he divorced the first woman, if he wanted to do so. If he divorced the second woman, then she had her second period, So these two were divorced and married, then God Almighty said to the third: {Then keep you in a fair manner or let him go in a good manner} so he divorces her. In that, it is recited in its entirety if she wishes, when she gathers her clothes."
"19566","(19566) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: It is only a separation and annulment. It is not a divorce. God mentioned divorce at the beginning of the verse and at the end, and divorce in between is not a divorce. God Almighty said: {Divorce is twice, then retain it with kindness, or let it go with kindness}"
"19567","(19567) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: Ikrimah said: Perhaps God will happen after that something. He said: What It happens after the third."
"19568","(19568) Ibn Abi Ghaniyyah told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak: {Perhaps God will happen after that something} He said: Perhaps he will return to her in the waiting period."
"19569","(19569) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Dawud al-Awdi, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: {You do not know, perhaps God will speak after that. A matter} He said: We do not know, perhaps you will regret it and have a way to come back."
"19570","(19570) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: If he divorces secretly, he takes him back secretly, then he will return to you secretly. If it takes place, there is no problem, but if he divorces her publicly and takes it back, then he should bear witness to her taking her back."
"19571","(19571) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: If he divorces secretly, he takes him back secretly."
"19572","(19572) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: A man had intercourse with his wife, then he died leaving her. At the end of her waiting period, he said: She is waiting for eleven months."
"19573","(19573) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: Khula is an irrevocable divorce, and she did not stipulate that it should be divorced. So it is for her."
"19574","(19574) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The divorce is the divorce of a mother. I promised her the same as the mother."
"19575","(19575) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The maintenance is on the one whose water you wait for."
"19576","(19576) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Whether the husband or wife is stoned, it is for his companion. Among them is inheritance."
"19577","(19577) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ali, who said: If he is stoned, then the inheritance is due to her."
"19578","(19578) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man marries a woman, and then she commits adultery, I will judge her. The punishment, and if she dies under the lash, her heirs."
"19579","(19579) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, about a man who appointed four witnesses against His wife said: She committed adultery. He said: She will be stoned and he will inherit her."
"19580","(19580) Muadh bin Muadh told us: Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who slandered his wife when she was young, he said: There is no punishment or curse upon him."
"19581","(19581) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Al-Zuhri about a man He married a woman on the condition that her affairs were in the hands of a man. Al-Hakam said: It is nothing. Al-Zuhri said: Yes, and Sufyan said: His opinion. Al-Zahri’s opinion."
"19582","(19582) Hakam al-Razi told us, on the authority of Anbasa, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq, who said: If a man says to his wife: You can be divorced if you want. He gave her the choice."
"19583","(19583) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, about a woman who married a man and stayed with him for years. Then her husband came and took her, and the other divorced her, saying: There is no divorce for him."
"19584","(19584) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Every corrupt marriage that is not valid is not valid. Divorce is divorce."
"19585","(19585) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Salih bin Muslim, who said: I asked Al-Sha’bi, I said: A man and his wife ruled by two men, then It seemed to them that they would return. He said: That is for them as long as they do not speak, but if they do speak, it is not for them to return."
"19586","(19586) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayoub, who said: I said to Sa`id Ibn Jubayr: How is cursing? He said: Take what is in the Qur’an: I bear witness in God, I bear witness in God."
"19587","(19587) Muhammad bin Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, saying: Amr bin Maimun narrated to us, on the authority of his father, who said: Umm Kulthum was under Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam, and he was a harsh man towards women. She thought of him and asked him to divorce her while she was pregnant, but he refused, so when He divorced her once, and she insisted on divorcing him, so he divorced her once while he was performing ablution, then he went out and a man overtook him. So he told him that Umm Kulthum had given birth. He said: She deceived me, God deceived her. So he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he mentioned that to him and told him what she had done, and he said: He preceded the Book of God concerning her. He proposed to her and said: She will never return to him.\n(Ibn Majah 2026. Bayhaqi 421)"
"19588","(19588) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he divorces a slave, he is not obligated to do so. Enjoyment"
"19589","(19589) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: If he is divorced, or emancipated In his dream, he is nothing."
"19590","(19590) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Ali, who said: The pen was raised, on the authority of The sleeper until he wakes up. (Abu Dawud 4401. An-Nasa’i 7345)"
"19591","(19591) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The pen was lifted, on the authority of three, from the sleeper until he wakes up.\n(Ibn Majah 2041. Ahmed 100)"
"19592","(19592) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, about a man who had four wives, and she joined them. One of them is in the war house. He said: He will divorce her, then he will marry her."
"19593","(19593) Ishaq Al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Al-Hasan, about a man who said to his wife: If you enter the house of so-and-so, you He was divorced and the house was demolished. He said: If the house was demolished, it is not a divorce. Ibn Hashim said: If the house was in the man’s possession and it was demolished. Or it was a way of marriage and she entered into it, and the divorce had occurred to her."
"19594","(19594) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: I bear witness that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He has divorced"
"19595","(19595) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: He divorced the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Two women, one of them from Bani Amir."
"19596","(19596) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Prophet did not divorce, but he He retires."
"19597","(19597) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar, that he married a woman from Banu Makhzum He was barren, so he divorced her, then he said: He did not indulge in pleasure with women, so if it were not for a child, she would not want them."
"19598","(19598) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abu Hilal narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, that Omar married a woman, and behold, he was a hag. So he divorced her."
"19599","(19599) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Qays bin Abi Hazim, who said: Khalid bin divorced The newborn to his wife, and he said: I did not divorce her for a past matter, but no calamity befell her with me."
"19600","(19600) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi, and Abdullah bin Ubaidah and Umar ibn al-Hakam reported that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, married a woman from the Banu al-Jun, so he divorced her and he From which she sought refuge.\n(Bukhari 5254, Ibn Majah 2037)"
"19601","(19601) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Salam bin Qasim al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Umm Sa`id: A secret woman who belonged to Ali. She said: Ali said: O Umm Saeed, I longed to be a bride. She said: He had four wives with him at that time, so I said: He divorced. He took one of them and replaced it, and said: Divorce is ugly, I hate it."
"19602","(19602) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, on the authority of al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The immoral women are the hypocrites. (Ahmad 2/414, Bayhaqi 316)"
"19603","(19603) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid and Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: Any woman who asks her husband for a divorce without any objection will not smell the scent of Paradise."
"19604","(19604) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, on the authority of Abu Asma, on the authority of Thawban, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similarly. (Abu Dawud 2221. Ahmad 5/283)"
"19605","(19605) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Shaqri, that a woman had her vagina removed. He married her off, and Abraham said: I will dispute with you before God on the Day of Resurrection."
"19606","(19606) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abu Hilal narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraida, who said: Omar bin al-Khattab said: If he wanted Women are divorced, so do not disbelieve them."
"19607","(19607) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, who said: Omar said: Do not force your girls to do so. The ugly man, for they love of that what you love."
"19608","(19608) Waki’ told us: Bashir bin Salman told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I like to adorn myself. For a woman, just as I like for a woman to be adorned for herself, because God Almighty says: (And they are like those who are obligated to do good.) And I do not like to take away my rights from her, because God Almighty says: {And men have a degree over them}"
"19609","(19609) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam: {And men have a level above them} He said: Imāra."
"19610","(19610) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad: (And for men there is a degree) He said: I do not know except that: (And for them Like those upon them) if they knew that degree."
"19611","(19611) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abu Malik: (And for the men there are degrees) He said: He divorces her and she has nothing to do with the matter."
"19612","(19612) Shababih told us, on the authority of Warqa’i, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: (And for men there are degrees) he said. The favor of God, what God favored him over her of jihad, and preferred his inheritance over her inheritance, and everything that he preferred. Aliyah"
"19613","(19613) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Habib bin Abi Thabit narrated to us, saying: I asked al-Hakam and Mujahid about a man. He had a woman with whom he had consummated the marriage, and he married another woman over her, and his first wife said: I will make a mount for you. That you divorce me once, and that you divorce this wife of yours, so he did, and the arbitrator said: They will all be divorced, and Mujahid said: She was the woman with whom he had not consummated the marriage, and he divorced the other woman.\n Waki` said: And the people are of the wise opinion."
"19614","(19614) Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, who said: He complained. Abraham went to his Lord to ward off Sarah’s character, so God Almighty revealed to him, “Indeed, the woman is like a rib, so if she straightens it You break it, and if you leave it it becomes crooked, then wear on what was in it."
"19615","(19615) Dhudha bin Khalifa narrated to us, saying: Awf narrated to us, on the authority of a man, who said: I heard Samurah bin Jundub giving a speech to Minbar al-Basra says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: The woman was created from a rib, and if she wants The end of the rib is broken, so its end is supported by it, so its end is supported by it. (Ibn Hibban 4178, Hakim 174)"
"19616","(19616) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Talq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aws bin Tharayb, who said: I hated Al-Hajjaj, so I entered The Sacred Mosque, then they saw Omar and Jarir. He said: Then Omar said to Jarir: O Abu Amr, how do you deal with your wives? He said: O Commander of the Faithful, I have faced severe hardship from them, and I cannot enter the house of any of them other than... Her day, and I do not kiss the son of any of them other than her mother’s day except that they become angry. He said: Then Omar said: Many of them do not believe. In God, nor does he believe in the believers. Perhaps you are in need of one of them and she misses you. He said: Then Abdullah bin Masoud said And he is among the people: O Commander of the Believers, do you not know that Abraham complained to God in order to ward off Sarah’s behavior? He said: So it was said: He said: The woman is like a rib. If you straighten it, you will break it, and if you leave it, it will become crooked. So dress your family according to what is in them. He said: Then Omar said to Abdullah: There is very little knowledge in your heart. He said it three times, and some of his companions added to it. I think it was Sufyan: as long as he did not see any damage to her religion."
"19617","(19617) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Misra, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Treat women well, for women were created from a rib, and the crookedest part of the rib is If you lose its straightness, you will break it, and if you leave it, it will remain crooked. Be careful of women. (Bukhari 3331. Muslim 60)"
"19618","(19618) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Rukain, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Hanzali, who said: Jarir bin Abdullah Ali came Omar complained to him about the bad behavior he had received from the women. He said: Then Omar said: I will receive the same as what you received from them. I will come. He said: The market or the people. I buy from them an animal or a dress. The woman says: He just went off to look at their girls, or to give a speech. To them, he said: Then Abdullah bin Masoud said: Do you not know how much of a defect Abraham doubted about Sarah’s character, so God revealed to him : It is only a rib, so take the rib and straighten it. If it is straight, otherwise wear it according to what is in it."
"19619","(19619) Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, who said: I asked Abraham about miscarriage, and he said: The waiting period is ended because of it."
"19620","(19620) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hasan narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amir, who said: Miscarriage is in the same position as a full-term child."
"19621","(19621) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of al-Hasan and Muhammad, who said: If the free woman aborts, her waiting period has expired."
"19622","(19622) Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq told us, he said: Husayn bin Waqid told us, he said: Abu Manazil told us, he said: I heard Shariha says: If a woman has a miscarriage, her free will be counted, and her concubine will be freed."
"19623","(19623) Ishaq Al-Azraq narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Harith that he said regarding the divorced woman and the deceased On the authority of her, if she abandons her child before she is fully created, he said: If anything becomes clear about her, she is permissible for the husband. He said, and Ibn Shubramah said: Until he becomes clear and knows that he is his son."
"19624","(19624) Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, who said: Al-Hasan used to say: If a clot of blood was thrown at him, or if he had chewed gum after It is known that it is a pregnancy, then there is a stranger in it and the waiting period is ended because of it, and if it is the mother of a child, then she is freed."
"19625","(19625) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, he said: Khaled bin Wardan told us, he said: I asked Ata’ about two men, each of them swore. From them: I did not say that, and under one of them is my aunt. He said: “We will talk to each other.”"
"19626","(19626) Muhammad bin Sawa narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, about a man who said to his wife: If I am close to you for a year, then you are divorced. He said: If he is close to you before the four months have passed, then he is divorced for three years. He left her until four months had passed, when she had departed from him by one time, and he could marry her if he wanted, but not get close to her. Until the year passes."
"19627","(19627) Muhammad bin Sawa told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He offered it before four days had passed. Months, then he divorced three times, but if he leaves her until four months have passed, then she has divorced him for one year. He can marry her if he wants, and have intercourse with her before the year is over."
"19628","(19628) Muhammad bin Sawa told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He offered it before the four days had passed. Months, then he is divorced for three, and if he leaves her until four months have passed, then she has separated from him by one, and no He will marry her until a period of less than a year has passed, two months, or three months, and he will marry her. He should not approach it until the year has passed, and that is Sa’id’s opinion."
"19629","(19629) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, who reported it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: It is not permissible for a woman to mourn over a dead person for more than three days, except for a husband. (Muslim 65. Ahmad 6/37)"
"19630","(19630) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Humaid bin Nafi’ that he heard Zainab bint Umm Salama narrates that she heard Umm Salama and Umm Habibah mentioning that a woman came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then she mentioned that her husband had died from a son of hers, so she complained about her condition and wanted to perform kohl on her, so the Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: One of you used to throw a het at the beginning of the year, but it was four. A month or ten. Humaid said: So I asked Zainab: Why did she throw the camel? She said: There was a woman in pre-Islamic times who went to the worst house of hers, and she sat there for a year. When the year had passed, She went out and threw a bunch of sand behind her. (Muslim 61. Tirmidhi 1197)"
"19631","(19631) Muhammad bin Fudayl and Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Safiyya. The daughter of Abi Ubaid said that she heard Hafsa, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrating that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: It is not permissible for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn more than three dead people, except for a husband. (Ahmad 6/286. Tabarani 361)"
"19632","(19632) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Umm Atiyya, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: There is no mourning period for a dead person for more than three days, except for a woman who must mourn for her husband for four months and ten days, and she does not wear clothes. Dyed clothing, except dyed clothing. Do not use kohl or apply perfume except at least to purify it with a piece of cloth or nails.\n(Bukhari 5342, Muslim 1128)"
"19633","(19633) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Majlis, who said: Ibn Umar said: Her husband died. The waiting period is four months and ten days, and a man said: This is a lot, and Ibn Umar said: The pre-Islamic people used to specify More than this."
"19634","(19634) Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Safiyya bint Abi Ubaid that She informed him that she heard Umm Salama, Aisha and Hafsa saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is not permissible No woman who believes in God and the Last Day mourns a dead person for more than three days, except for her husband, in which case she mourns him. Four months and ten days. (Muslim 1128)"
"19635","(19635) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he did not see mourning as anything."
"19636","(19436) Hafs bin Ghayath and Ali bin Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abu, who said: It is a matter of trust that a woman is entrusted with her private parts."
"19637","(19637) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abu, who said: Trust is that a woman has been entrusted with her private parts."
"19638","(19438) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: relief Amen."
"19639","(19639) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: It is a matter of trust that a woman is entrusted with Her relief"
"19640","(19640) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Ayoub Al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, who said: He mentioned He had a number of women, so he said: We were not commanded to open them."
"19641","(19641) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Amir, who said: A woman came to Ali and he divorced her. He married her off, so she claimed that she had her menstruation in the third month of menstruation, and she purified herself at every recitation and prayed. Then Ali said to Shurayh: Say And Shurayh said: If a woman from your family comes among those who are satisfied with her religion and her trustworthiness, they will bear witness. She menstruated three menstrual periods in a month, and she purified herself at every time of Quran and prayed, so she was telling the truth, otherwise she was lying, so he said. Ali: They said, and he held thirty in his hand, meaning the Romans."
"19642","(19642) Ismail bin Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Jalad bin Ayyub, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurayh, on the authority of Anas, who said: Qurayh Menstruation: four, five, six, seven, eight, nine, ten, then you wash and pray."
"19643","(19443) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas, who said: Do not be The woman undergoing menstruation for one day, or two days, or three days, until she reaches ten days. If she reaches ten days, then Mustahaza."
"19644","(19644) Ismail bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Umm Al-Dahhak bint Rashid, who said: I heard Khaled bin Ma’dan say: The least you can be A woman's menstruation lasts for three days, the last of which is ten days."
"19645","(19645) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Ali bin Thabit, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr said: Menstruation is twelve days."
"19646","(19646) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The maximum period for a menstruating woman to sit is fifteen nights."
"19647","(19647) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Menstruation is fifteen days."
"19648","(19648) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Read it as long as she is menstruating."
"19649","(19649) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Muqasim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, was sent to his dead person and appointed Zaid. If Zaid was killed, then Ja’far, and if Ja’far was killed, then Ibn Rawahhi. He said: Then Ibn Rawahih remained behind to gather with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw him and said: He did not leave you behind. He said: I agree with you, and he said: Your morning, or your soul in the path of God, is better than this world and what is in it.\n(Tirmidhi 1439. Ahmad 1/256)"
"19650","(19650) Waki` narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl ibn Sa`d, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: A morning, or a soul spent in the path of God is better than this world and what is in it. (Bukhari 2794, Muslim 114)"
"19651","(19651) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Ayyub, who said: Sharhabeel bin Sharik narrated to us. Al-Maafiri, on the authority of Abu Abdul-Rahman Al-Hubali, said: I heard Abu Ayyub saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: For his morning in the path of God, or his soul, is better than what the sun rises and sets upon. (Muslim 1115. Ahmad 5/422)"
"19652","(19652) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: A morning or a soul in the path of God is better than this world. (Bukhari 27931 1500)"
"19653","(19653) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Marawahih, on the authority of Abu Dhar, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, which work is best? He said: Faith in God and jihad in His path. (Bukhari 2518, Muslim 136)"
"19654","(19654) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Al-Eizar, on the authority of Saad bin Ias Abi Amr Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdullah, said: I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Which work is best? He said: Prayer at its appointed time. He said: I said: Then what? He said: Being kind to parents. He said: I said: Then what? He said: Jihad in the path of God."
"19655","(19655) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, who said: The example of a fighter in the path of God is the example of one who He fasts during the day and prays at night until the invader returns, whenever he returns. (Ahmad 4/272, Bazzar 3222)"
"19656","(19656) Affan narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: : A morning or a night spent in the path of God is better than this world and what is in it. (Bukhari 2792, Muslim 1499)"
"19657","(19657) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Salama bin Sabra, on the authority of Salman, he said: If the man For the sake of God, let his heart tremble with fear, and his sins fall away just as the stem of a palm tree opens.\n(Tabarani 6086. Ibn Al-Mubarak 35)"
"19658","(19658) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: I heard Urwah ibn al-Nazzal narrating on the authority of Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: We came with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from his invasion of Tabuk, and I said: O Messenger of God, tell me about its climax. He said: As for the peak of Islam, it is jihad in the way of God, meaning the peak of Islam. (Ahmad 5/237 Tabarani 305)"
"19659","(19659) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: God has guaranteed that he who sets out on His path out of faith in Him and out of belief in His Messengers will enter him. The jinn, or He will return him to his abode, obtaining the reward or spoils he obtained. (Bukhari 36 Muslim 107)"
"19660","(19660) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, they said: They said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, tell us about an act that equates to jihad in the path of God. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: You cannot endure him. They said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, inform us, so perhaps we can endure him. He said: For example The one who strives in the path of God is like a fasting person who is obedient to the signs of God. He does not stop fasting or giving alms until he returns. Mujahid to his family.\n(Bukhari 2787, Muslim 110)"
"19661","(19661) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: I had hoped not to leave behind a convoy that would go out in the path of God, but I do not have it. I cannot bear them, and I wish to be killed in the way of God, then brought back to life, then killed, then brought back to life, then killed.\n(Bukhari 2972, Muslim 1497)"
"19662","(19662) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Zur’i, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: God has prepared for those who go out in My path that they will not go out except to strive in My path and have faith in Me. And believing in My messengers, I am guaranteed that I will admit him to Paradise, and that I will return him to the abode from which he emerged as a recipient. What reward or spoils he obtained, he said: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, had I not made it difficult for the Muslims, I would not have stayed in disagreement. A group that will fight in the path of God forever, but I will not find a way to carry them, nor will they find a way to follow me, nor will I If they please themselves, then they will fall behind after me. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I would have liked to fight in the path of God and be killed, then I invade and be killed, then I invade and be killed.\n(Muslim 1496. Ahmad 2/231)"
"19663","(19663) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, Mujalid bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Wadak, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, it is narrated that The hadith said: There are three whom God laughs at: a man when he gets up during the night to pray, and a people when they line up for prayer. When the people line up to fight the enemy, (Ahmad 3/851 Abd ibn Humaid 911)"
"19664","(19664) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I heard Ruba’i narrating on the authority of Zayd ibn Dhabyan. It was transmitted to Abu Dharr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: There are three whom God loves, so he mentioned: One of them is a man. He was in a company and they met the enemy and were defeated, so he attacked him until he was killed, or his chest was opened for them. (Ahmad 5/153. Ibn Hibban 3350)"
"19665","(19665) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his commanders and Hamid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: There is no soul that dies for which God is better than it would be for it to return to the world, nor that it has the world. There is nothing in it except the martyr, and he wishes to return and be killed in the way of God, because of the virtue of the martyr he sees. (Bukhari 2817, Muslim 108)"
"19666","(19666) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Anas, who said: A woman came to him whose son had been killed, and he did not She had someone else, and her name was Harithah, so she said: O Messenger of God, if he is in Paradise, be patient. If it is other than that, then you will know what I will do? Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Indeed, there are many gardens and he is in the highest paradise. (Bukhari 3982)"
"19667","(19667) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Fudayl, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The witnesses are Ali Bariq: a river at the gate of Paradise in a green dome. Their provision from Paradise will be paid out to them morning and evening. (Ahmad 1/2668 Ibn Hibban 4658)"
"19668","(19668) Ibn Adiy told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Hilal Ibn Abi Zainab, on the authority of Shahr Ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Abi Hariri, he said: The martyrs were mentioned before the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: The earth will not dry up from the blood of the martyr until His two wives rush forth as if they were two female goats who had led their flocks astray across vast expanses of land, and in the hand of each one of them. A solution better than the world and what is in it. (Ahmad 2/427)"
"19669","(19669) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, they said: O Messenger of God, which jihad is best? ? He said: Whoever slays his horse and sheds its blood. (Darimi 2392, Ibn Hibban 4639)"
"19670","(19670) Wakī’ narrated to us, Al-Masoudi narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Harith, on the authority of many On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: A man said: O Messenger of God, which jihad is best? He said: Whoever slays his horse and sheds its blood.\n(Tayalisi 2272)"
"19671","(19671) Waki` narrated to us, Usama bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Bajaj bin Abdullah al-Janni, on the authority of Abu Huraira, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A time will come upon the people when the best of people will be in rank. Whoever takes the reins of his horse in the path of God, whenever he hears about it, he will sit on his board, then seek death in his place. And a man in one of these peoples, who performs prayer and pays zakat, and leaves people except for good. (Muslim 1271, Ibn Hibban 4600)"
"19672","(19672) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Abi Zayd, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: A man came from The Prophet went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that you are His servant. And His Messenger, then he advanced and fought until he was killed, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He did this easily and was rewarded abundantly. \n(Bukhari 2808, Muslim 144)"
"19673","(19473) Zaid bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Sulaiman al-Dab’i, Abu Imran al-Juni narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa Al-Ash'ari said: I heard my father, facing the enemy, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: : Swords are the keys to Paradise, and a shabby man said to him: O Abu Musa, did you hear this from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? May God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, so he unsheathed his sword, broke its sheath, turned to his companions, and said: I extend my greetings to you, then he advanced to the enemy and fought. Until he was killed. (Muslim 146 Tirmidhi 1459)"
"19674","(19674) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Yazid bin Shajara rose Among his companions, he said: Indeed, it has become upon you of something between green, red, and yellow, and in the houses what is in them, So when you meet the enemy tomorrow, move forward, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Not a single step forward. Unless the young virgin comes forward to him, and if he delays, he will hide from him, and if he is martyred, it will be his first sacrifice of expiation for his sins. And two young virgins come down to him, shake off the dirt from him, and say to him: Welcome, the time has come for you, and he says: Welcome, the time has come for you. They punched you\n(Tabarani 642, Musnad 527)"
"19675","(19675) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Musa Abi Ja’far Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Sabrah bin Abu Fakih, who was one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: : Satan sat for the son of Adam with his ways, so he sat for him with the path of Islam, and said: Will you become a Muslim and abandon your religion and the religion of your fathers? Then he sat with him on the way to migration, and he said: You migrate and give up your birth and become like a horse in its length. Then he sat with him. By the way of jihad, and he said: You wage jihad, and you are killed, and you marry your wife, and your inheritance is divided? He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever does that, God guarantees him Paradise if he is killed, or dies by drowning, or Burned, or eaten by seven beasts.\n(Bukhari 2431. Tabarani 6558)"
"19676","(19676) Zaid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd Allah ibn Atik, on the authority of his father, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: He who goes out to fight for the sake of God, then he brought his three fingers together, then said: And the Mujahideen groaned, so he fell down from his mount and died, for his reward has fallen upon God. Or he is bitten by an animal, then his reward falls on God. And whoever dies without his nose, his reward falls on God. And whoever is killed recklessly, his reward falls on God. It was necessary to return. (Ahmad 4/368 Hakim 88)"
"19677","(19677) Shababi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Saeed bin Khalid, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Dhu’ayb, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to them while they were sitting. He said: Shall I not tell you about the best of people in rank? We said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: A man holding the head of his horse in the way of God until he is killed or dies. Shall I inform you of what follows? They said: Yes, O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: A man who isolates himself among a people who performs prayers and pays zakat. He avoids the evil of people. (Nasa’i 2350, Darmi 2395)"
"19678","(19678) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Ismail ibn Umayyah, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas added to it Ibn Idris, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: When your brothers were afflicted, God placed their souls in the bellies of green birds, to which the rivers of the jinn flow. And you will eat its fruits and roam in Paradise wherever you wish. So when they saw their good abode, their food and their drink, they said: If only our people knew what God has done for us, so that they would desire jihad and not turn away from it. Then God said: God Almighty: Indeed, I will inform you and inform your brothers, so rejoice and rejoice in that. That is what God Almighty says: {And do not think that They were killed in the cause of God as dead, but rather they are alive and provided with their Lord.\n(Abu Dawud 2512, Ahmad 1/265)"
"19679","(19679) Waki` narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu Iyas Muawiyah bin Qurayh, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Every nation has a rabbi and a rabbi, this nation is jihad for the sake of God\n(Saeed bin Mansour 2309)"
"19680","(19680) Waki’ narrated to us, Thawr narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Awf, on the authority of Mujahid bin Riyah, on the authority of Ibn Omar said: Shall I not inform you of a night better than the Night of Decree? A sentinel on the path of God Almighty, in a land of fear, hoping that he will not return to his family. (Nasa’i 8868)"
"19681","(19681) Waki` narrated to us, Ali bin Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Amer al-Uqaili, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The first three to enter Paradise, The martyr, a chaste and self-controlled man with dependents, a servant who is the best of servants to his Lord, who fulfills the rights of his master, and the first of three They will enter Hell as an authoritative prince, someone with wealth who does not pay his due, and a poor and proud person. (Tirmidhi 1442. Ahmad 2/479)"
"19682","(19682) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zina, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, says: Indeed, God laughs at two men, one of whom kills the other. Both of them enter Paradise, and they fight. This one is in the path of God and will be martyred, then God will turn to his killer and he will surrender, and he will fight in the path of God. He will be martyred.\n(Muslim 1505. Ahmad 2/244)"
"19683","(19683) Waki’ narrated to us, Mugheerah bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, people have invaded, and something has detained me, so guide me to a job. He joined me with them and said: Are you able to pray the night prayer? He said: Can you afford that? He said: Are you able to fast during the day? He said: Yes, he said: Your prayer during your night and your fast during your day are like the sleep of one of them."
"19684","(19684) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Thumama Ibn Abdullah Ibn Anas, on the authority of Anas, who said: I came Ali Thabit bin Qais on the Day of Al-Yamamah while he was mummified, so I said: Uncle, don’t you see what the people encountered? He said: Now, my nephew. Now, my nephew."
"19685","(19685) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Suda, and he recited these verses: {And the predecessors The forerunners are those who are brought near. He said: They are the first of them to go to the mosque, and the first of them to go out in the path of God Almighty."
"19686","(19686) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiyya, on the authority of Farwa Al-Lakhmiy, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Any woman who goes out and comes back and has failed will have her reward twice."
"19687","(19687) Issa narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiyya, who said: Whoever spends the night guarding the night has already morning. His sins have been forgiven, Al-Awza’i said, and Makhoul said: He spent the night until morning, his sins had been forgiven."
"19688","(19688) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Amr Al-Sibani, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Knight gored him, or two, and then there will be no knight after that ever. And the horned Romans are the companions of the sea and the rocks. Whenever a century goes away, a generation takes its place. Your companions, whatever is good in life. (Harith 702)"
"19689","(19689) Bishr ibn Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Amara ibn Abi Hafsiya, on the authority of Hijr, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr: {Then someone was struck by shock. In the heavens and whoever is on earth except whom God wills."
"19690","(19690) Issa told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Amr al-Saskiki, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr, who said: When The grief of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, became intense for those who were afflicted with Zayd on the day of his death. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And peace be upon him: The Messiah will surely bring you forth from these nations people who are like you, or better, three times, and he will not be disgraced. God is the mother, I am the first, and the Messiah is the last. (Hakim 41)"
"19691","(19691) Waki’ narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Hafs, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He recited on the Day of Badr: {Race to forgiveness from your Lord and a garden whose width is the heavens and the earth} Mas’ar said: Either that which is in the family of Imran, or Which is in iron? Ibn Qusham said: If you conquer, O Messenger of God, what will be the reward for whoever meets these people and fights until he is killed? He said: The jinn. He said: Sufficient for me is this world. And in his hand were dates, so he threw them. Then he came forward and was killed.\n(Muslim 145, Ibn Al-Mubarak 77)"
"19692","(19692) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Nu’aym ibn Abi Nad, a man said: On the Day of al-Qadisiyah: Oh God, my haddiyat is black, so marry me today to a beautiful virgin. Then he came forward and was killed. He said: So they passed by him while he was embracing a great man."
"19693","(19693) Waki` narrated to us, Mis`ar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`d bin Ibrahim, who said: They passed by a man on the Day of Qadisiyah who had His hands and feet were cut off, and he was examined, and he said: “With those upon whom God has bestowed blessings, of the prophets and the truthful.” And the martyrs and the righteous, and those are good companions.} Then the man said: Who are you, O Abdullah? He said: I am a man from the Ansar."
"19694","(19694) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Alqamiya ibn Marthad, he said: Whoever heard Umar ibn Abd narrated to me Al-Aziz, he said: A woman passed by while her son and her husband had been killed, so she came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: You are the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and God has sent down the revelation to you. If these two were hypocrites, we would not cry over them. And We did not favor them in kind, and even if they were not hypocrites, we said about them what we knew. He said: Yes, they were not hypocrites. They have met with the fruits of Paradise, and the angels have interacted with them. He said: The woman says: Now it is right that I should not make you cry. He said: : Indeed, you are with them.\n(Abdul Razzaq 6692)"
"19695","(19695) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah, who said: A man passed by on the Day of Qadisiyah. His shin, or his stomach, spread out, and he said to some of those who passed by him: Join me from him, come close to the chain of a spear, or two spears in it. For the sake of God, he said: So he passed by him, and he did so."
"19696","(19696) Waki’ narrated to us, Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Ala’, the father of Harun Al-Ghanawi, on the authority of a man, it is said Narrated by Muslim bin Shaddad, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, who said: The martyrs are in domes in a garden in a courtyard. The jinn, a whale and a bull will be sent to them, and they will have fun with them. If they need something, one of them will bruise its companion. So they ate from it and found the taste of everything from heaven."
"19697","(19697) Waki’ narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Yazid bin Shajara, who said: Swords are the keys to Paradise. So, if a man approaches the enemy, the angels say: O God, help him, and if he delays, they say: O God, forgive him. So first A drop of the blood of the sword will drip, with which he will be forgiven for all sins, and two stars will descend upon him, wiping the dust from his face. And they say: The time has come for you, and He says to them: And the time has come for you."
"19698","(19698) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, he was asked: Which deeds are better or better? He said: Faith in God and His Messenger. It was said: Then what? He said: Jihad in the way of God. It was said: Then what? He said: Hajj Mabrur. (Bukhari 26. Muslim 135)"
"19699","(19699) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The best martyrs are those who are thrown into a row and do not turn their faces until they are killed. Those are confused. In the highest rooms of Paradise, your Lord laughs at them. Indeed, when your Lord laughs at a people, there is no reckoning with them.\n(Tabarani 4143, Harith 633)"
"19700","(19700) Abu Asama told us, Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, he said: I saw a man He wanted to buy something for himself on the Day of Yarmouk, and his wife was pleading with him. He said: Repel this from him. If only I knew that I will afflict her with what I want as long as I did not suffer from her. By God, if I were able, a day would not pass that this would disappear from its place. And he pointed with his hand to a mountain, so if you overpower my body, take it. Qais said: So we passed by it, and we saw it after that. He was killed in that battle."
"19701","(19701) Abu Usama told us, he told us like a whisper, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of Ibn Al-Ahmas, he said: I said to Abu Dharr: A hadith that has informed me about you. On the authority of the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Come, I do not think I would lie to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted him after I heard it from him. He said: I said: I mentioned three whom God loves. He said: I heard it and said it. As for the one who loves By God, a man meets a group and a group is discovered, so he fights behind them until he is killed, or God grants victory for him, and a man is captured with them. A people who loved to touch the earth, so they encamped, and he stood up to pray until he woke them up with their departure, and a man who had an evil neighbor. So he was patient when he hurt him. (Ahmad 5/151)"
"19702","(19702) Abu Asama told us, Ismail told us, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Mudarrak ibn Awf Al-Ahmasi, he said: I was with Omar, when the messenger of Al-Numan bin Muqrin came to him, and Omar asked him about the people, and he said: So-and-so and so-and-so and others I do not know were injured, so Omar said: But God knows them, so he said: O Commander of the Faithful, and a man who sold himself, so Mudrik bin Awf said: That is, by God. My uncle, O Commander of the Faithful, the people claimed that he was thrown into ruin with his own hands, so Omar said: Those people lied, but he was among those who He bought the hereafter for this world."
"19703","(19703) Waki’ narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Salma bin Sabra, on the authority of Salman, he said: When the servant crawls For the sake of God, his sins were placed on his head, opened just as the stem of a palm tree opens."
"19704","(19704) Waki’ narrated to us, Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sulayman, on the authority of Anas, he said: I heard him say: His morning in The path of God is better than ten Hajj for those who have performed Hajj."
"19705","(19705) Waki’ told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Adam bin Ali, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Omar say: A journey. It means that one campaign in the path of God is better than fifty Hajj."
"19706","(19706) Waki’ narrated to us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Sha’ithi narrated to us, on the authority of Makhoul, he said: In Paradise there are hundreds of A degree, what is between one degree to another, just as the distance between the heavens and the earth, God has prepared it for those who strive in the path of God.\n(Bukhari 2790, An-Nasa’i 4340)"
"19707","(19707) Waki` narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, he said: The first verse to be revealed from the Paras is: {Go forth, light and heavy. And strive with your wealth and your souls in the way of God}"
"19708","(19708) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh narrated to me, Qays ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, on the authority of Hanash ibn Ali. Al-Sana'ani, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying in the words of God Almighty: {Those who spend their wealth by night and day, secretly and openly} He said: On horses for the sake of God."
"19709","(19709) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Raja’ ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Musa al-Dimashqi narrated to us, that he heard Sahil bin Ajlan Al-Baili said in the words of God Almighty: {Those who spend their wealth by night and day, secretly and openly} He said: On horses in the way of God. He said: Then he mentioned that whoever ties a horse in the way of God has not tied it out of sight or hearing. He was among those who spent their money day and night."
"19710","(19710) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, the client of the family of Talha, on the authority of Isa bin Talha, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: No dust will ever gather in the way of God, nor the smoke of Hell in the nostril of a servant, and no man will ever enter Hell. He cried out of fear of God until the milk entered the udder. (Tirmidhi 1433. Ahmad 2/505)"
"19711","(19711) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Qutba bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Salem Ibn Abi Al-Ja’d said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was shown to them in sleep, and he saw Ja’far, an angel with two wings, spread out. With blood, and Zaid was facing him on the bed, and Ibn Rawahhi was sitting with them, as if they were turning away from him.\n(Tabarani 1468 and Ibn Hibban 7047)"
"19712","(19712) Malik bin Ismail narrated to us, Zuhair narrated to us, Dawud bin Abdullah Al-Awdi narrated to us, that his father Abba Karz Al-Harithi narrated that he heard Al-Rabi’ bin Zayd saying: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was walking, he It was a young boy from Quraysh who was walking away from the road, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Isn’t that so-and-so? They said: Yes, he said: So call him. He said: Why did you withdraw from the path? He said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I hate dust. He said: So do not isolate yourself from it, for by the one who is the soul of Muhammad In his hand, it is the offspring of Paradise. (Abu Dawud 3050, An-Nasa’i 8819)"
"19713","(19713) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Musa ibn Abi Uthman, on the authority of Abu Al-Awwam, on the authority of Abu Ayyub He stayed away from jihad for one year, so he recited these verses: {Go forth, light and heavy.} So he fought during his year, and he said: I did not see In these verses, it is a concession."
"19714","(19714) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Malik, who said: The first thing that was revealed from Bara’ih was: {Go forth. Light and heavy}"
"19715","(19715) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Abu Salih: {Go forth, light and heavy} He said: The old man and the young man."
"19716","(19716) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: old and young, his leaders said: active. And not active."
"19717","(19717) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam: {Go forth, light or heavy.} He said: Mashaghil. And other things."
"19718","(19718) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: The old man and the youth."
"19719","(19719) Shababah told us, on the authority of Warqa’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: {Go forth, light and heavy} He said: Among us. The heavy, the needy, the weak, and the busy."
"19720","(19720) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: old and young."
"19721","(19721) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever fasts a day for the sake of God will be saved from Hell for a hundred days. (Nasa’i 2562)"
"19722","(19722) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sumayyah, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Abi Ayyash, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No servant fasts a day for the sake of God, except that God will compensate for that. Today, seventy days have passed from the face of the Fire. (Bukhari 2840. An-Nasa’i 2561)"
"19723","(19723) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Nu’man, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, something similar, but he did not narrate it."
"19724","(19724) Waki’ narrated to us, Al-Rabi’ bin Subaih narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Aban, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever fasts a day in the way of God, God will keep him away from Hell for seventy years. (Ibn Adi 717)"
"19725","(19725) Waki` narrated to us, Qais narrated to us, on the authority of Shimr ibn Atiyya, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, He said: Whoever fasts a day for the sake of God, there will be between him and Hell a ditch farther than what is between the heavens and the earth."
"19726","(19726) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, who said: I heard Yaqub bin Asim bin Urwa bin Masoud narrates on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: In Paradise there is a palace, called Eden, in which there are five thousand gates on each... There are five thousand chapters, with five thousand ink on each chapter. He said, “Ali, I will calculate it.” He said, “No one will enter it except a prophet, or A friend, or a witness."
"19727","(19727) Waki` narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq: {Those are the truthful ones. And the martyrs} He said: This is exclusively for the martyrs."
"19728","(19728) Waki’ told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, he said: specifically for the martyrs."
"19729","(19729) Waki` narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, who said: The martyr will have six characteristics on the Day of Resurrection: He is safe from the punishment of God and from the greatest terror, and he intercedes for such-and-such from his household, and he is made lawful. Faith, and he will see his place in Paradise, and all sins will be forgiven. (Bukhari 642. Ahmad 4/200)"
"19730","(19730) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Alqamah, who said: One battle for one who has performed Hajj is better than ten days. Hajjat q"
"19731","(19731) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Masruq, he said: I asked Ibn Masoud, about These verses: {And do not think that those who are killed in the way of God are dead; rather, they are alive with their Lord and are provided with.} Then He said: Are we not? We asked about that, and he said: Their souls are like green birds, roaming about in Paradise, whichever way they wish, then they take refuge there. A lamp hung from the throne. While they were like that, when their Lord appeared to them and said: Ask Me whatever you wish, and they said: O Our Lord, what do we ask of you, while we roam in Paradise in whichever way we wish? Their Lord informed him, and he said: Ask me whatever you want, so they said: O our Lord, and what do we ask of you while we are rejoicing in Paradise in the same place? As we wish, he said: While they were like that, their Lord looked upon them and said: Ask of Me whatever you wish, so they said: O our Lord. And what do we ask you, while we are roaming around in Paradise in whichever place we wish? He said: When they saw that they would not be left behind, they said: We ask you. To return our souls to our bodies to this world until we are killed in your cause. He said: When he saw that they only asked This one left them.\n(Muslim 1502 and Ibn Majah 2801)"
"19732","(19732) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Salem ibn Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Shurahbil ibn Al-Samat, he said: We said to Ka’b ibn Murah: Tell us, O Ka’b, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and beware, and he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Shoot with an arrow at anyone who reaches the enemy, for which God will raise him in rank, so Abdul Rahman said to him Ibn Abi Al-Nahham: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, what is the staircase? He said: She is not your mother’s threshold, but there are a hundred years between the two degrees. O Ka’b, tell us about the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace, and beware. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Whoever turns gray for the sake of God will grow old. It will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever shoots an arrow in the way of God will be like one who freed a slave. (Tirmidhi 1434, Ahmad 4/235)"
"19733","(19733) Waki’ narrated to us, Muhammad bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith bin Al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Malik bin Abdullah Al-Khath’ami, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever’s feet become dusty in the path of God, God will make him sacred to the Fire.\n(Bukhari 907, Ahmad 5/226, Tabarani 661)"
"19734","(19734) Waki` narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Yahya bin Amr bin Salama narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: Abdul said God: Because I enjoy using a whip in the way of God is more beloved to me than Hajj after Hajj."
"19735","(19735) Waki` narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Qais, he said: I heard Sa`d say: I am the first Arab to throw an arrow into For the sake of God"
"19736","(19736) Zaid bin Harun told us, I am Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, On the authority of his father, he said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, because you were killed in the path of God. Did God expiate your sins? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If you are killed in the way of God, patient and seeking reward, coming forward and not retreating, God will disbelieve in him. Your sins except debt. This is what Gabriel said to me."
"19737","(19737) Zaid bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, Abdullah bin Abi Qatada narrated to us, on the authority of his father, He said: When we arrived from our invasion of Tabuk, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who among you met any of those who remained behind? He does not speak to him or sit with us."
"19738","(19738) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Yunus bin Saif, on the authority of Umair bin Al-Aswad, who said: Omar said: You must perform Hajj, for it is a righteous deed that God has commanded, and jihad is better than it."
"19739","(19739) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said about heaven. A palace called Aden, with winds and towers around it, and five thousand gates. No one can live in it, or no one can enter it except a prophet, or A truthful person, a martyr, or a just imam."
"19740","(19740) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Zirr, who said: Abdullah said: Sleepiness during killing is a security from Allah. And at the time of prayer from Satan, he recited these verses: {When drowsiness overtook you, out of security from it}?"
"19741","(19741) Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Samimi told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, that Abu Talhah used to throw stones between The hand of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, behind him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is raised up. He bowed his head, and Abu Talha raised his head, saying: We will sacrifice, but not you, O Messenger of God. (Bukhari 3811, Muslim 136)"
"19742","(19742) Abdullah bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Abu Talha, he said: I was among those who were sent down. He must be sleepy on the day of Uhud. (Bukhari 3811, Tirmidhi 3007)"
"19743","(19743) Affan narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zubair, something like Hadith of Abu Talha (Tirmidhi 3007)"
"19744","(19744) Abu Asama narrated to us, Mus’ab bin Sulaym al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Anas bin Malik narrated to us, he said: When he was sent Abu Musa Ali Al-Basra was among those with whom Al-Bara’ was sent, and he was one of his ministers, and he used to say to him: Choose from your work, and he said: Al-Bara’: And you gave me what I asked you? He said: Yes, he said: I do not ask you for the leadership of Egypt, nor for its tax, but give me my bow and my spear, and my horse and my sword. And my shield, and jihad in the path of God. He sent him to lead an army, and he was the first to be killed."
"19745","(19745) Abu Asama told us, Mus’ab bin Sulaym told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: Al-Bara’ imitated a line of poetry, so I said: To him: My brother, you imitated a line of poetry, not knowing whether it might be the last thing you spoke? He said: I will not die on my bed, I have killed a hundred men of the polytheists and hypocrites, except one man."
"19746","(19746) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, that his uncle was absent from the battle of Badr, so he said: I was absent from the first fight that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fought, by God, because God showed me the fighting of the polytheists so that I could see them. God, what should I do? When it was the day of Uhud, the Muslims were discovered, and he said: Oh God, I apologize to you for what these people, meaning the Muslims, have done. And I absolve you of what these people, meaning the polytheists, have brought to you. Then he went forward and Saad met him with the last part without anyone else, so Saad said to him: I am with you. Saad said: I was not able to do as he did. Twenty-one people were wounded with a sword and stabbed with a spear. And he shot an arrow at him, and we used to say: about him and his companions. The verse was revealed: {And among them is he who has died, and among them is he who waits}? (Bukhari 2805, Muslim 1512)"
"19747","(19747) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Thuban, Hassan bin Atiyya narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Munib Al-Jurshi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I was sent before me to strike with the sword until... God alone is worshiped, with whom nothing is associated, and my provision has been placed under the shade of my spear, and humiliation and indignity have been made upon those who disobey My command, and whoever imitates a people is one of them. (Abu Dawud 4027. Ahmad 2/50)"
"19748","(19748) Affan narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Mara, on the authority of Abdullah, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Our Lord is astonished by two men: a man who rose from his bed and quilt from among his love, and his family rose to Him. His prayers, desiring what I have, and fearing what I have, and a man who fought in the cause of God Almighty and his companions fled, so he knew what He had no choice but to flee, but he had no choice but to return, so he returned until his blood was shed. Then God Almighty says to His angels: Oh, my angels. Look at my servant, who returned until his blood was shed, desiring what is with me and yearning for what is with me. (Abu Dawud 2528, Hakim 112)"
"19749","(19749) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God reclined God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was with his son Malhan. He said: Then he fell asleep and woke up smiling. He said: She said: O Messenger of God. May God bless you, what made you laugh? He said: There are people from my nation who invade this Green Sea, like them like kings over captives. He said: She said: O Messenger. God, pray to God to make me one of them. He said: Oh God, make her one of them. He said: So Ubadah had intercourse with Ibn al-Samit, and she rode with him. His son Qarza, and when she stopped and killed her animal, she killed it and then buried it.\n(Bukhari 2788, Muslim 160)"
"19750","(19750) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Muslim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr said: It is more beloved to me to undertake a campaign on the sea than to spend an acceptable quintal in the path of God Almighty."
"19751","(19751) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Alqamah bin Shihab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever is not able to fight with me, let him fight in the sea, for one invasion of the sea is better than two forays into the sea. And the martyr of the sea will have the reward of the martyr of land. Indeed, the best of the martyrs in the sight of God are those who stand alone. They said: O Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and who are the Companions of the Waqf? He said: A people whose vehicles are sufficient for them in the path of God. (Abdul Razzaq 9631)"
"19752","(19752) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of those who heard Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr said: He who floats in the sea is a conqueror like one who is drenched in his blood, a martyr on land."
"19753","(19753) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, an informant told me, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr said: One expedition at sea is better than ten expeditions on land. Whoever crosses the sea as a conqueror, it is as if he had crossed All valleys."
"19754","(19754) Abu Asama told us, Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Ibn Abbas went out invading. In the sea and I am with him."
"19755","(19755) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: No one should ride the sea except a pilgrim, or a traveler, or Congregationalist."
"19756","(19756) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that Omar Ibn Al-Khattab said: I am amazed at the one who sails the sea, and I am amazed. For a merchant who migrated."
"19757","(19757) Waki’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: God will not ask me about An army that never took to the sea. It means deception."
"19758","(19758) Yahya bin Abi Bakir narrated to us, Hariz bin Uthman narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Misra, on the authority of Abi Rashid Al-Habarani, he met Al-Miqdad sitting on one of the coffins of the money changers, and he had leftover a bone, so I said to him: I have May God excuse you, O Abu Al-Aswad. He said: Surah Al-Huth has rejected us, meaning Surah of Repentance: {Go forth, light and heavy}"
"19759","(19759) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: My father, who breastfed me from the children of Mara, told me: It is as if I were looking at Jafar. On the day of his death, he dismounted from a horse that had a blonde hue, and hobbled it, then he went on and fought until he was killed. (Abu Dawud 2566, Hakim 209)"
"19760","(19760) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Amr ibn Utbah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, He said: I came to Abdullah bin Mukhramama, who was suffering from an epilepsy in the year of Al-Yamamah, and I stood over him, and he said: O Abdullah bin Omar, may he break his fast? The fasting person? I said: Yes. He said: Make water for me during this ordeal so that I may break my fast. So I went to the basin and it was full of blood, so I hit him with my fist. Then she drifted off into it, came to him, and found that he had finished."
"19761","(19761) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hashim bin Hashim, I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab say: Saad bin Abu Waqqas is the most powerful of the Muslims on the Day of Uhud."
"19762","(19762) Muawiyah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Khaled Al-Walbi, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra. He said: The first person to shoot an arrow in the way of God was Saad."
"19763","(19763) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Habiba, on the authority of Abu Darda’, that a man He recommended something for the sake of God, and said: It will be given to the Mujahideen."
"19764","(19764) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shimr, on the authority of Shahr, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, he said: Whoever fasts One day, in the path of God, there was a ditch between him and the Fire as between the heavens and the earth."
"19765","(19765) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Mus’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja’di, he said: Omar said: Were it not that I walk in the path of God, or put my side in the dust for God, or sit with people who enjoy good words. Just as the perfume of dates is picked, I would love to have joined God."
"19766","(19766) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Qais, he said: I heard Khalid bin Al-Walid say: He may He prevented me from reciting a lot of prayers and striving for the sake of God."
"19767","(19767) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Ziyad, on the authority of Khalid bin Al-Walid, who said: What There was a night on earth, in which I was given good tidings of a boy, and a bride was presented to me. I am a lover of hers, more beloved to me than the night. The severity of the ice in a group of immigrants has caused the enemy to attack them, so you must wage jihad."
"19768","(19768) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Eizar bin Harith, he said: Khaled said: Ibn Al-Walid, by God, I do not know what day I will flee from? On the day that God wanted to guide me to martyrdom, or on the day that God wanted to guide me on that day. Dignity"
"19769","(19769) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: I was informed that Abdullah bin Salam said: You have overtaken me and I have no strength, so carry me on a bed, meaning the battle, until you place me between the two rows."
"19770","(19770) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Al-Rukain bin Al-Rabi’ Al-Fazari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Yasir bin Umayla, on the authority of Khurraym bin Fatik Al-Asadi, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Whoever spends will spend For the sake of God, seven hundredfold has been recorded for him. (Tirmidhi 1425. Ahmad 4/345)"
"19771","(19771) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, he said: Misra told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I asked Ka'b about the Garden of Refuge, and he said: As for the Garden of Refuge, it is a Garden in which there are green birds in which souls ascend. Martyrs"
"19772","(19772) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, Shayban told us, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Atiya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Mujahid in the path of God is guaranteed by God, or He will suffice him for His forgiveness. And His mercy, or that He will bring him back with a reward and spoils, and the example of one who strives in the path of God is the example of a fasting person who stands and does not falter. Until he comes back.\n(Ibn Majah 2754; Abu Ali 1331)"
"19773","(19773) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, Hariz bin Uthman narrated to us, Abu Munib Al-Jurashi narrated to us, that a man descended upon Tamim and traveled with him, and he saw that he had fallen short of what he had done to his family, so he said: May God have mercy on you, I see that you have fallen short of what he had done to his family. Were you with your family? He said: Is it not enough for me, that I have the reward of a fasting and standing person?"
"19774","(19774) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, Muhammad bin Sirin narrated to us, he said: Horses raided. To the polytheists on the streets of Medina. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out and came to Abu Qatada, and he had combed his hair. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I see that your hair is holding you back? He said: I will bring you a man who is safe. He said: And they liked to let their hair be free."
"19775","(19775) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Abi Husayn, on the authority of Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Salami, who said: Because Having a son who strives in the cause of God is more beloved to me than a hundred thousand."
"19776","(19776) Waki’ told us, Abu Al-Ashhab told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said Your Lord: Whoever goes out and strives in My Way to seek Your Face, then I am a guarantor for him. If I seize him in My Face, I will bring him in. The jinn, and if I bring him back, I will bring him back with the reward and spoils he gained. (Bukhari 36. Muslim 1495)"
"19777","(19777) Wakī’ narrated to us, Malik bin Mughal and Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Abu al-Za’ri, who said: Abdullah said: A time will come upon the people in which a man will be exalted with his little character just as he is exalted with his abundance of wealth. And his two sons. They said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, what is the best of the man’s wealth at that time? He said: A good horse and a good weapon will depart with the servant wherever they depart."
"19778","(19778) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, who said: Abu Ayyub invaded the land of the Byzantines and fell ill, so he said: : Since I am dead, if you join forces with the enemy, bury me under your feet. (An-Nasa’i 4420, Saeed bin Mansour 2450)"
"19779","(19779) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, he said: Abu Salam al-Dimashqi narrated to me, On the authority of Khaled bin Zaid, he said: I was an archer, and Uqba bin Amir would pass by me and say: O Khaled, take us out. Nermi, and one day she was late for him, and he said: O Khaled, come, I will tell you what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. And peace be upon him: God brings in with one arrow three people of the jinn: the one who made it, who expects goodness in his work, and the archer. And there is no distraction except in three things: a man’s training of his horse, his playing with his family, and his shooting with his bow and his arrow. And whoever abandons stoning after learning about it, then it is a blessing that he neglected, or disbelieved in it."
"19780","(19780) Issa bin Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us: My father told me, on the authority of men from Banu Salama, who said: When he spent Mu'awiyah is the same one that passes over the graves of the martyrs, so it was carried out on them, meaning on the grave of Abdullah bin Amr bin Haram, and on The grave of Amr bin Al-Jamouh was buried, and their graves emerged, and a cry was shouted over them, so We took them out two by two, as if they were They died yesterday, wearing two cloaks with which their faces were covered, and some of the Izkar plant on their feet."
"19781","(19781) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Qais, on the authority of Nabih, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Abu Abd said to me God: O my sons, had it not been for the forgotten women who succeeded me after me, daughters and sisters, I would have loved to present you before me, but be in The overseers of the city, he said: I did not wait until she brought her two dead paternal uncles, meaning his father and his paternal uncle, whom she presented to me. A camel\n(Bukhari 4052)"
"19782","(19782) Waki` narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr: {And do not think that those who were killed in In the way of God are the dead. Rather, they are alive with their Lord and are provided with.} He said: When Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib and Musab bin Umair were injured. On the day of Uhud, they said: I wish our brothers knew what good we have befallen, so that they would increase in their desire. Then God said: I will convey the message. About you, then it was revealed: {And do not think that those who were killed in the cause of God are dead, but rather alive with their Lord, being provided for, rejoicing} to His saying {the believers}"
"19783","(19783) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jabala, on the authority of Tawoos, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace And he said: God sent me with the sword in the hands of the pursuer, and He placed my livelihood under the shade of my spear, and He placed the humiliation and the small upon me. Whoever disagrees with me and whoever imitates a people is one of them. (Ibn Al-Mubarak 105)"
"19784","(19784) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he said to Saad bin Muadh while he was distressed with himself: May God reward you better than the leader of my people, for God has fulfilled what she promised him. And God is true to what He promised you. (Ibn Saad 429)"
"19785","(19785) Muhammad Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: A letter came from the East from Battalions of infidels, and a man from the Ansar met them and attacked them, breaking through the line until he left, then he said “Allahu Akbar” and returned and did the same. Twice, or three times, when Sa`d ibn Hisham mentioned that to Abu Hurairah, so he recited these verses: {And among the people are those He sells himself seeking God’s pleasure}"
"19786","(19786) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Abd al-Rahman bin Awf. He was brought with food. His people said: I think he was fasting. Abdul Rahman said: Hamza was killed, and we did not find anything to shroud him. And he is better than me, and Musab bin Umair was killed and he was better than me, and we did not find anything to support him. We were afflicted with what we were afflicted with. He said His people or he said: We give from it what we have been given. Then Abdul Rahman said: I fear that our good deeds have been hastened for us. This world, his people said: I think he rose and did not eat."
"19787","(19787) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Kammis narrated to us, on the authority of Sayyar ibn Manzur, on the authority of his father, he said: Ibn Abdullah bin Salam, he said: I was equipped as a fighter, and when I put my feet in the stitches, my father said to me, “Son, sit down.” I said: Wasn't this before I prepared and spent? He said: I wanted the reward of a fighter to be recorded for me, and it is a calamity coming from here, and he pointed with his hand towards the Levant. If I catch it, you will show me how to do it, but if I do not catch it, hasten on it."
"19788","(19788) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ubaid ibn al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, who said: Ibn Abd Allah ibn Greetings from the invasion, so his father turned to him and said: O my son, do not do it, for when the scream of Damascus comes it will reach every Muslim."
"19789","(19789) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: I heard Khalid ibn al-Walid say: It was pressed into my hand. On the day of my death, nine swords will strike me, and nothing will remain in my hand except a Yemeni plate."
"19790","(19790) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, Al-Masoudi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, asked him to give him a sword, and he said: Perhaps if I gave you a sword, you would use it to carry the sword. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him a sword and he began to strike the polytheists with it, saying:\n I am a man who pledged allegiance to my boyfriend while we were at the foot of the palm trees.\n Shall I not stand up all the time in the battlefield, striking with the sword of God and the Messenger?"
"19791","(19791) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythami, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: He will come. There will be a period of time upon the people, when no believer will remain unless he joins the Levant."
"19792","(19792) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Al-Kharit, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It was obligatory upon the Muslims that a man from among them should fight ten polytheists, as God Almighty said {Indeed There will be twenty of you who are steadfast. They will defeat two hundred, and if there are a hundred of you, they will defeat a thousand.} So the part of that. upon them, so God sent down relief, and appointed upon a man fighting the two men, as God Almighty says: {And if there be a hundred of you patient, they will prevail. Two hundred} So that was lightened for them, and they were short of victory in proportion to that. (Bukhari 4452, Abu Dawud 2639)"
"19793","(19793) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr Al-Ghasani, on the authority of Habib bin Amr, who said: Ka’b said: I love The land to God is the Levant, and the most beloved of the Levant is Jerusalem, and the most beloved of Jerusalem is Mount Nablus. There will come a time when people will touch each other. Between them with ropes."
"19794","(19794) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyyah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: The stronghold of the Muslims from the epics is Damascus, and their stronghold from the Antichrist is the Holy House, and their stronghold from Gog and Magog. House of Tur. (Hakim 462. Ibn Asakir 232)"
"19795","(19795) Yahya bin Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya bin Ayyub narrated to me, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Shamasa al-Mahri informed him, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: While we were around the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. We compose the Qur’an from the fragments. He said: Blessed is the Levant. Blessed is the Levant. It was said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And why? He said: Because your angels, the Most Gracious, spread their wings over you. (Tirmidhi 3954, Ibn Hibban 114)"
"19796","(19796) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiyya, who said: Mal Makhul, and Ibn Zakariya To Khalid bin Maadan, and I turned with them, and he told us on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr. He said: Jubayr said to me: Go with us to Dhu. Mukhammar, and he was a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I went with him, and Jubayr asked him about the truce, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: The Romans will make peace with you in a secure settlement, then you and they will fight an enemy and be victorious. And you take spoils and deliver them, then you leave until you come down to a meadow with high hills, and a Christian man raises the cross. Then he says: The cross prevailed, and a man from among the Muslims becomes angry and goes up to him and strikes him. Then the Romans will betray and gather For the epic (Abu Dawud 2761 and Ibn Hibban 6708)"
"19797","(19797) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah, on the authority of his sheikhs, he said: Omar said: Save the nails. In the enemy's land, it is a weapon."
"19798","(19798) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, he said: If it was presented You must invade, so do not choose Armenia, for there is a torment from the torment of the grave."
"19799","(19799) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: We invaded the land of the Romans and with us Hudhayfah, and we had a man from Quraysh over us. He drank wine, so we wanted to challenge him. Hudhayfah said: You are defying your emir, and he... You come close to your enemy and they seek you. He said: We will drink it, even if it is forbidden, and I will drink it in spite of... In spite of"
"19800","(19800) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Mu’tim bin Al-Miqdam, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: So It is linked to three, so let the worshipers worship what they wish."
"19801","(19801) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Hisham bin al-Ghaz, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Salman, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: A day’s fast in the path of God is better than a month’s fasting and standing in prayer, and whoever dies while stationed will be rewarded with The grave was tempted, and his good deeds continued until the Day of Resurrection. (Muslim 1520, Ahmad 5/440)"
"19802","(19802) Issa ibn Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, who said: Ata al-Khurasani narrated to me, on the authority of my father. He saw a similar word, except that he said: the coast of the sea. (Ibn Majah 2767. Ahmad 2/404)"
"19803","(19803) Yahya bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Aqeel, on the authority of Abu Salih, the servant of Uthman. Ibn Affan, on the authority of Uthman, that he said on the pulpit: O Muslims, I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Recently, I concealed your hatred because you were separated from me. I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Ribat A day in the path of God is better than the bond of a thousand days in other dwellings, so let each person choose for himself what I wish\n(Tirmidhi 1467. Taalisi 87)"
"19804","(19804) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Dawud bin Qais narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Abdul Rahman Al-Asqalani, on the authority of Abu Huraira said: The completion of the bond will take forty days. (Saeed bin Mansour 2410)"
"19805","(19805) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Yahya al-Sadfi, on the authority of Yahya bin al-Harith al-Dhamari, on the authority of Alcoholic, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The bond is forty days. (Tabarani 7606)"
"19806","(19806) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Abdullah, the client of Ghafari, who said: A man from the descendants of Abdullah bin Omar, that a son of Ibn Omar intermarried for thirty nights, then came back, and he said to him: Ibn Omar: I intend for you to come back and stay together. Ten until you complete forty."
"19807","(19807) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, he said: Khalid bin Ma’dan told us, he said: I heard Abu Umamah and Jubayr bin Nufir said: There will come upon the people a time when the best of jihad is steadfastness, so I said: What is that? He said: When the invasion spreads, the debts are many, and the spoils are permissible, then the best jihad on that day is bondage. \n(Ibn Hibban 4856. Tabarani 334)"
"19808","(19808) Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Hamid bin Sakhr, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt and Safwan bin In good health, they said: Whoever dies as a marabout dies as a martyr."
"19809","(19809) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ibn Habib Al-Muharbibi, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bailili, He said: The conquests were won by people whose ornaments were not gold or silver, but rather their ornaments were made of gold. And incense and iron."
"19810","(19810) Al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ziyad bin Anam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever has his head cut off in the path of God, God will forgive him for his previous sins. His sin\n(Saeed bin Mansour 2425. Bazar 767)"
"19811","(19811) Yahya bin Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya bin Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Qabil, he said: I heard Abdullah Ibn Amr was asked: Which of the two cities will be conquered first, Constantinople or Rome? He said: So Abdullah bin Amr called for a box with a ring on it, and he took out a book from it and began to read it. He said: So he said: While we are We write about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he was asked: Which of the two cities should be conquered first: Constantinople, or Romans? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Rather, the city of Heraclius will be opened first. (Ahmad 2/1761 Hakim 422)"
"19812","(19812) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father and uncle, who heard them mention it. They said: Salman bin Rabi’a said: I killed with my sword a hundred Muslims, all of whom worship other than God. I did not kill a patient man among them."
"19813","(19813) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Musa bin Saeed, on the authority of his scholars, he said: Abu Musa said: He You saw me on the fifth of five days, or the sixth of six days, and there was no nail on my hand or any nail on my feet unless he prayed. Then he said: He did not differ from me. Mention this, may God reward me with that."
"19814","(19814) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: No one dies. There is nothing good for him with God that pleases him. He wishes to return to this world, and there is no bliss like it except the martyr. For from the reward he sees, he wishes that he could return and be killed. (Saeed bin Mansour 2554)"
"19815","(19815) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, who said: The martyr in the sight of God has six characteristics: May God forgive him. His sin is at the first drop of his blood that reaches the ground, and he is made to wear the garment of faith, and he is married to the free-eyed virgin, and the reward for him is opened. A gate from Paradise, a protection from the torment of the grave, and protection from the greatest terror or the terror of the Day of Resurrection."
"19816","(19816) Bishr bin Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah bin Habib, who said: I asked Salim about fighting, and he failed. Then he raised his head and said: {Indeed, God loves those who fight in His way in rows as if they were a solid building}"
"19817","(19817) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {And do not throw with your hands into Destruction} He said: Spend in the way of God, even if it is miserly."
"19818","(19818) Waki` narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: When you meet, stand up. This verse was revealed only about spending."
"19819","(19819) Muhammad bin Marwan Al-Basri told us, on the authority of Amara, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was cut open and broken. He was thirsty until he fell on his knees, and his companions left him, so Ubayy ibn Khalaf came to ask With the blood of his brother Umayyah ibn Khalaf, he said: Where is this who claims to be a prophet? Let him come to me, for if he is a prophet They killed me, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: They gave you the war. They said: O Messenger of God, are you free? He said: Indeed, God has asked for his blood to drink, so he took the spear, then walked to him and stabbed him, so he threw him off his animal and carried him. His companions sought refuge for him and said: We do not see any harm in you. So he said: Indeed, God has asked for my blood to be poured. Indeed, I find it as if it had been upon him. Mudar and Rabi'ah, You will encompass them. \n(Bukhari 2911, Muslim 1416)"
"19820","(19820) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, Al-Hakam bin Mina narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah that He heard him say, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Your morning in the path of God, or your soul, is better than this world and what There it is.\n(Ahmad 2/532)"
"19821","(19821) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Malik bin Thalabiyah, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Hakam Ibn Thawban, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: What do you consider the martyr? He said, so they said: The one killed in the way of God. He said: Indeed, the martyrs of my nation are few, then the one killed in the way of God is a martyr and the last About his animal in the way of God is a witness, and drowning in the way of God is a witness, and stabbing in the way of God is a witness, And the one who is afflicted in the way of God is a witness, and the one who is afflicted in the way of God is a witness, meaning the ulcers of pleurisy. (Muslim 164. Ahmad 2/441)"
"19822","(19822) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, on the authority of Ubadah ibn Nasi, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: What do you think is the martyr among you? They said: The one who fights in the way of God and is killed. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The martyrs of my nation then For a little while, the one killed in the cause of God is a martyr, the stabbed one is a martyr, the one who is injured is a martyr, and the woman dies in a plural. It means pregnant and witness. (Ahmad 5/315, Darami 2414)"
"19823","(19823) Waki’ told us, Abu Al-Umays told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jabr bin Atik, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited him during his illness, and someone from his family said: We had hoped that his death would be He killed a martyr in the way of God, and he said: Indeed, the martyrs of my nation are few, then the one killed in the way of God is a martyr and the afflicted. A martyr, and the stabbed person is a martyr, and a woman dies with the plural of a witness, and burning and drowning, and the one who is stabbed is a witness, meaning an ulcer with the same The side\n(Ibn Majah 2803. Tabarani 1780)"
"19824","(19824) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Aamir bin Malik, on the authority of Safwan bin Umayyah, he said: The plague is a martyr, and drowning is a martyr, and the stomach and pneumonia are a martyr."
"19825","(19825) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: Abdullah said: Of those who drown in seas and are thrown back from mountains and eaten by wild beasts - they will be witnesses before God on the Day of Resurrection."
"19826","(19826) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of a stolen woman, on the authority of a stolen woman, who said: The plague And the stomach, and postpartum, and drowning, and whatever afflicts a Muslim, he is his witness."
"19827","(19827) Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Muhammad bin Jahad narrated to us, that Abu Husayn narrated to him, that Abu Salih He narrated to him, that Abu Hurairah narrated to him, saying: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, Teach me something that is equivalent to jihad. He said: I do not find it. He said: Will you be able, when the mujahid comes out, to enter your mosque and stand up? Do you break your fast and do not break your fast? He said: I cannot do that. Abu Hurairah said: The mujahid’s horse is not as long as it is long, so its good deeds are recorded for it. (Bukhari 2785. Ahmad 2/344)"
"19828","(19828) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: There is no man, or no one, who spends two wives in the way of God except that the jinn will protect him. On the Day of Resurrection, they will call upon Him: Come, O so-and-so, come. This is better. Then Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, this is better. The one who did not turn to him and said: I hope that you will be one of them. (Bukhari 1897, Muslim 85)"
"19829","(19829) Waki’ told us, Al-Rabi’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: A man said to Omar: O the best of people. He said: I am not the best of people. Shall I not tell you about the best of people? He said: Yes, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: A man from the people of the desert who has a camel or sheep that he brought to Egypt from among the lands. So he sold it, then spent it in the way of God, and he was among the Muslims and their enemy, so that is the best of people."
"19830","(19830) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Safwan ibn Sulaym, on the authority of Husain ibn Al-Lajlaj, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Stinginess and faith do not coexist in the heart of a Muslim man. There is no dust in the way of God, nor the smoke of Hell in the belly of a man. (Ahmad 2/342, Hakim 72)"
"19831","(19831) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Salim who raises him to Muadh, he said: Whoever is young A gray hair in the way of God will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever shoots an arrow in the way of God, God will raise him up with him. Degree\n(Tirmidhi 1438. Ahmad 4/113)"
"19832","(19832) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, who said: There is no better case. That the servant should be answered in it, unless he is in the path of God, rather than being helpless, with his face prostrating."
"19833","(19833) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: Al-Zubayr converted to Islam when he was sixteen years old, and he did not He is left behind from a campaign. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, invaded him and was killed when he was sixty-odd years old."
"19834","(19834) Waki’ narrated to us, Hisham bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, he said: When Abu Ubaidah al-Sham was besieged, he and his companions and their wounded were in great distress. He said: So he wrote to Omar, and Omar wrote to him: Greetings. On you, as for what follows, there was never a hardship without God making a way out after it, and no hardship will be overcome by ease, and He wrote To him: {O you who have believed, be patient and steadfast, and be united and fear God that you may succeed} He said: So Abu wrote to him `Ubaydah: Peace be upon you. Now, God, Blessed and Most High, said: “Know that the life of this world is only play, amusement, and adornment.” And boasting among you and multiplying in wealth and children} until the end of the verse, he said: Then Omar came out with the letter of Abu Ubaidah and read it to him. The people, and he said: O people of Medina, Abu Ubaidah only wrote to confront you and urge you to jihad. He said Zaid: Then my father said: I was standing in the market when a bright people came, who had emerged from the city, and among them was Hudhayfy ibn al-Yaman. They give good tidings to the people. He said: So I went out and became stronger until I came to Omar and said: O Commander of the Faithful, give good tidings of God’s victory and conquest. Omar said: God is Greatest if he had been Khalid ibn al-Walid."
"19835","(19835) Waki’ told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, God has provided for this nation in the teeth of its horses and the sharpness of its spears unless they are planted, but when they are planted they become among the people."
"19836","(19836) Affan narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Kathir, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, on the authority of Ata bin Zayd, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, it was said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, which of the believers is best? He said: A believer who strives in the cause of God with his life and his wealth, and a believer who isolates himself in a mountainous area, or his people said: Enough of people's evil.\n(Bukhari 2786. Muslim 122)"
"19837","(19837) Affan narrated to us, Ubaid Allah bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Kabsha Al-Bara’ bin Qays. Al-Sakouni said: I was sitting with Saad while he was speaking to his companions, and he said at the end of his hadith: O people, God intended I am more beloved to you than two Hajjs, and two Hajjs are more beloved to me than two Hajjs. Performing Hajj to the House of God is more beloved to me than two Umrahs, and performing Umrah is more beloved to me than three days to the Holy House."
"19838","(19838) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh narrated to me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn al-Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Firas Yazid bin Rabah, client of Amr bin Al-Aas, said that he heard Abdullah bin Amr say: God laughs at the companions of The sea repeatedly, when it leveled itself in its boat and left its family and possessions, and when the sea took it in its boat. And when righteousness directs him and he looks up to him. (Ibn Khuzaymah 343)"
"19839","(19839) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab Al-Ataridi, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He greeted: If he was in line during the battle, he did not turn around."
"19840","(19840) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Othman bin Ghayath, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: I heard him say in these verses: {And “You say of those who are killed in the cause of God, ‘They are dead,’ nay, they are alive, but you do not perceive.” He said: The souls of the martyrs are in white, bubbling birds. In heaven"
"19841","(19841) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Atik, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: As for what he likes of vanity, it is the man. He flaunts with his sword when fighting and when giving charity, and he does not like to have fun. (Abu Dawud 2452. Ahmad 5/445)"
"19842","(19842) Zayd bin Hubab told us, Musa bin Ubaidah told me, he said: Muhammad bin Abi Mansour told me, on the authority of Al-Samit bin Abdullah, on the authority of Salman, that he was among a Muslim army, and besiegement and hardship befell them, so Salman said to Amir Soldier: Shall I not tell you what I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that will be of help to you against this soldier? I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: Whoever fasts a day or a night in the path of God, then his fasting is just. The month and its prayers are the one who does not break his fast, nor departs except for a need. And whoever dies while still in the path of God will be rewarded with his reward. Until God decides between the people of Paradise and Hell. (Musnad 455)"
"19843","(19843) Zaid bin Hubab narrated to us, Abu Sinan Saeed bin Sinan narrated to us, he said: Musa bin Abi Kathir informed me. Al-Ansari, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, said in the words of God Almighty: {Who is the one who lends to God a good loan?} He said: spending in the way of God."
"19844","(19844) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, Musa bin Ubaidah told us, Ayoub bin Khalid Al-Ansari told us in His saying: {Who is the one who lends to God a good loan}? Okay"
"19845","(19845) Zaid bin Hubab told us, Musa bin Ubaidah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Hakim bin Hizam. He said: Whoever spends two pairs in the way of God, no gate of Paradise will come to him except that it will be opened for him. Then Moses said: I heard. Our sheikhs say: two pairs: a dinar and a dirham, or a dirham and a dinar."
"19846","(19846) Zaid bin Hubab told us, Musa bin Ubaidah told me, he said: Abdullah my brother told me, on the authority of my father. Shaybāb al-Mahri and Mudrak said: No dust in the path of God, nor the smoke of Hell, will gather in the chest of a believer."
"19847","(19847) Zaid bin Harun told us, Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, he said: The souls of the martyrs are in birds. Khadr will wander in Paradise and take refuge in lamps suspended from the Throne, and then your Lord will appear to them and say: Ask me three times. He says it, and they say: Our Lord, we ask you to bring us back to this world so that we may be killed in your cause another way."
"19848","(19848) Zayd bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, he said: Muadh bin Afraa: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, why does the Lord make His servant laugh? He said: He dipped his hand into the enemy while he was naked. He said: He threw away the armor he was wearing and fought until he was killed. (Bayhaqi 99)"
"19849","(19849) Zaid bin Harun told us, Hariz bin Othman told us, on the authority of Nimran bin Mikmar Al-Rahbi, he said: Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah was marching with the army and saying: There is no God who bleaches his clothes desecrates his religion."
"19850","(19850) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Bashar bin Abi Saif, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Iyad bin Ghataif, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Whoever spends virtuously in the way of God, the reward will be seven hundredfold."
"19851","(19851) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, Thabit bin Yazid narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Maymoon, Omar said: Hajj is here. Then he points with his hand to Mecca, then I go out in the way of God Almighty."
"19852","(19852) Dhudha bin Khalifa told us, Awf told us, on the authority of Khasna bint Muawiyah, she said: My uncle told me, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who is in Paradise? He said: The Prophet is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, and the one who is resurrected is in Paradise. (Abu Dawud 2513. Ahmed 58)"
"19853","(19853) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa, he said: I heard Musa bin Talhah say: Talhah was wounded with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He received twenty-five wounds. (Saeed bin Mansour 2849)"
"19854","(19854) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: Whoever sets out in the path of God, seeking the face of God, and fulfilling God’s promises, then he is like The fasting person who continues until he returns to his family, or from where he left. (Ahmad 2/4651 Ibn Hibban 4621)"
"19855","(19855) Khaled bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abd al-Aziz, al-Zuhri narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ka'b bin Malik, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no wounded person who is wounded in the way of God except that he comes His wound on the Day of Resurrection will be blood, its color will be the color of blood, and its scent will be the scent of musk. Present the Qur’an to most of the people and make it In the grave (Bayhaqi 11)"
"19856","(19856) Ali bin Ubaid told us, Abu Hayyan told us, on the authority of a sheikh from the people of Medina, who said: He was among me. The writer of Ubayd Allah ibn Muammar was well-known for his friendship, so I asked him to copy the letter of Abdullah ibn Ubayy to me. Awfa told Ubaidullah. He said: So they copied it for me, so it was in it. Abdullah bin Abi Awfa narrated on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Do not ask to meet the enemy. If you meet them, be patient and know that the Garden is under the shade of Swords and he was waiting, and when the sun had passed, he would call out to his enemy and say: O God, who sends down the Book and causes the clouds, And defeat the parties. Oh God, defeat them and grant us victory over them. (Bukhari 2966. Muslim 20)"
"19857","(19857) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad, he said: Fadl The one who invades the sea over the one who invades the land is like the superiority of the one who invades the land over the one who sits in his house."
"19858","(19858) Shababi told us, Laith bin Saad told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Abi Al-Khattab, on the authority of Abi Saeed Al-Khudri, that he said that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed the people in the year of Tabuk, which was Leaning his back against a palm tree, he said: Shall I not inform you of the best of people and the worst of people? Among the best of people is a man who carries in the path of God on the back of his horse, or on the back of his camel, or even on his feet. Death will come to him, and among the worst of people is an immoral man who reads the Book of God and does not heed any of it. (Ahmad 3/37 Hakim 67)"
"19859","(19859) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd bin Jud’an, he said: Abu Talha said: (Go forth, light and heavy.) He said: old and young. He said: I do not see God excusing anyone. So he went out to the Levant and fought jihad."
"19860","(19860) Zaid bin Harun told us, Ibn Awn told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Al-Ajafa Al-Salami, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab said: Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever is killed in the way of God, or dies, will be in Paradise.\n(Ahmad 1/400 Hakim 175)"
"19861","(19861) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Abdul Aziz bin Omar narrated to us, Yazid bin Yazid bin Jabir narrated to me, on the authority of Anecdotally, on the authority of some of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that supplication was recommended when the rain descended and it was established. Prayer, and the meeting of the two rows."
"19862","(19862) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Sadiqa bin Al-Muthanna, who said: I heard my grandfather Riyah bin Al-Harith mentioning on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Zayd Ibn Amr Ibn Nufayl says: By God, there is no witness. A man of them will witness one day in the path of God with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, whose face is covered with dust is better than the work of any of you, even if it lasts as long as Noah.\n(Ibn Abi Asim 1435)"
"19863","(19863) Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, Ja’far bin Abi Kathir told us, Al-Ala bin Abdul Rahman bin Yaqoub told me. On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: An infidel and his killer will not meet. Muslims in Hell. (Muslim 1505. Abu Dawud 2487)"
"19864","(19864) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Wasil bin Al-Sa’ib Al-Raqqashi, who said: Ata bin Abi Rabah asked me: What? Is there a creature written on you? He said: So I said: A horse. He said: That is the ultimate reward. Then he mentioned that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Shall I not inform you of the most beloved of God’s servants after the prophets, the truthful ones, and the martyrs? He said: A faithful servant, with his spear resting on his horse, tilting it sleepily to the right and to the left in the path of God, seeking forgiveness from the Most Gracious. And Satan is cursed. He said: And the gates of heaven are opened, and God says to His angels, “Look at my servant.” He said: Then they ask forgiveness for him. He said: Then he recited: {Indeed, God has purchased from the believers their lives and their wealth so that they will have the jinn, and they will fight in the way of God} Until the end of the verse."
"19865","(19865) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash`ath bin Siwar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah Bin Hudhayfah, he said: Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, Abdullah bin Masoud, Abu Masoud Al-Ansari, and Abu Musa were Al-Ash'ari was in the mosque, and a man came and said: O Abdullah bin Qais, so he called him by his name, and said: Have you seen if I took My sword, so I struggled with it, seeking the face of God, so I was killed while I was doing that. Where am I? He said: In Paradise. Hudhayfy said: Then the man inquired and he understood, so let them enter the Fire. Such-and-such will do. What? He said this? Then Hudhayfah said: If you take your sword and strive with it and achieve the truth and are killed while doing that, then you will be in Paradise, and whoever The truth was wrong and he was killed while doing that, but God did not grant him success or protect him, and he entered the Fire. The people said: You have spoken the truth. (Abdul Razzaq 9565)"
"19866","(19866) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: They used to say: Fighting in the way of God. It is better than sitting, and sitting is better than fighting against misguidance, and whoever is tempted by anything should move on to that which he does not doubt."
"19867","(19867) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of al-Bara’ bin Aazib, he said: When These verses were revealed: {Not equal are those who sit among the believers, other than those in need of harm and those who strive in the path of God} The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Call for Zaid for me and he will bring the tablet and the medicine, or he said: with the shoulder, so he said: Write {No Those who sit are equal to the believers. He said: Ibn Umm is mute and was blind. O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. What do you command me to do, since I cannot fight? So God revealed in its place: {Other than those who suffer harm}"
"19868","(19868) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: The martyrs were mentioned at the time of Omar. Ibn Al-Khattab said: Then Omar said to the people: What do you think of the martyrs? The people said: O Commander of the Faithful, they are among those who will be killed in these battles. He said: Then he said: Then your martyrs are Many, I will tell you about that: Courage and cowardice are instincts in people that God places wherever He wishes, so the brave He fights behind someone who does not care that he does not return to his family, and the coward flees from his mistress, but the martyr is the one who He sought the reward for himself, and a muhajir is one who abandons what God has forbidden, and a Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand Muslims are safe."
"19869","(19869) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, that the first man to draw a sword in... For the sake of God, Al-Zubair, he was defeated, the Messenger of God was taken, and Al-Zubair came out and cut people with his sword, and the Messenger of God was in the highest place. He said: Then he met the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: What is the matter with you, Zubair? He said: Were you told that you were taken? He said: He prayed for him and prayed for him and for his sword. (Abdul Razzaq 20429. Ahmad in the Virtues of the Companions 1266)"
"19870","(19870) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, Shuabi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Fayd, he said: I heard Saeed bin Jabir Al-Ra'aniyy, on the authority of his father, that Abu Bakr sent an army and walked with them, and said: Praise be to God, our feet are covered with dust. For his sake, he said: Then a man said: We only sent them on their way, and he said: We only prepared them, sent them on their way, and called for them."
"19871","(19871) Ibn Abi Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qays, or others. It is considered doubtful on his part. He said: Abu Bakr sent an army to the Levant, and he went out to accompany them on foot, and they said: O Caliph. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, if you ride, he said: I will be held accountable for my sins in the path of God."
"19872","(19872) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: When Ikrimah bin Abi Jahl converted to Islam, he came The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: O Messenger of God, by God, I will not leave the position of my lofty position to be diverted from the path of God except I have done something like it in the path of God, and I will not let go of what I spent to turn it away from the path of God unless I spend something like it. For the sake of God, when it was the day of Yarmouk, he descended, dismounted, and fought fiercely, and was killed. Seventy-odd people were found with him. Between stabbing him, throwing him, and hitting him. (Tabarani 1022, Hakim 642)"
"19873","(19873) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, Hisham bin Saad narrated to us, he said: Qays bin Bishr Al-Taghlabi narrated to me, he said: My father was a companion of Abu Darda’ in Damascus, and he was in Damascus a man from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. It is said: He had Ibn al-Hanzaliyya from the Ansar, and the man was a loner. He rarely sat with people, but he only prayed, so when he left, It was only glorification and rejoicing, until his family came. One day he passed by us while we were with Abu Darda’ and he greeted us. Then Abu Al-Darda’ said to him, “Say a word that will benefit us and will not harm you.” He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The one who spends on Horses in the path of God, like one who spreads his hand with charity and does not seize it, then he passed by us another day and greeted, so Abu said Al-Darda': A word that will benefit us and will not harm you. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You are coming against your brothers. So put your saddlebags in order and put on your clothes, so that you will be as if you were a disgrace among people, for God does not like indecency. And indecency.\n(Abu Dawud 4086. Ahmad 4/179)"
"19874","(19874) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid said: Come with us in the morning until we make food. He said: So I went to him in the morning, and he said to me: Yesterday I recited Surah Bara’a and I found her urging people to wage jihad. He said: So he left."
"19875","(19875) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Ibn Umar in Al-Ja’aliyah: I do not sell my share. Of jihad, and I will not fight for any reward."
"19876","(19876) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubair bin Adiy, on the authority of Al-Shaqiq bin Al-Aizar, he said: I asked Ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of the Ja’ayel, and he said: If you take it, then spend it in the way of God, and leave it is better. I asked Ibn Umar, and he said: I will not take bribes except what God has given me."
"19877","(19877) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn al-Ajam, who said: I asked Ibn Abbas about The camels, he said: If you put them on a weapon, or a sheep in the way of God, then there is no problem. He said: Even if you put them on a male or female slave It is useless."
"19878","(19878) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Utba, who said: He came out There was a mission among the people during the time of Muawiyah, so Muawiyah wrote to Jarir bin Abdullah: Indeed, we have removed the mission from you and from your sons. So Jarir wrote to him: I have pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to listen, obey, and be sincere to the Muslims. We will go out there, otherwise we will strengthen those who will go out. (Bukhari 571 Muslim 97)"
"19879","(19879) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Al-Aswad was asked about the man who makes... For him and make it less than what was made for him and will it be better? He said: There is no problem, and Shurayh was asked about that, and he said: Leave what doubts you for what does not doubt you."
"19880","(1988) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdulaziz, on the authority of Makhoul, that he did not consider making In the tribe, he is powerful."
"19881","(1981) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Maadan bin Hudayr al-Hadrami, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr Al-Hadrami, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Like those of your nation who wage war. And they take the camel to strengthen themselves against their enemy, just like the mother of Moses breastfeeding her children and receiving her reward. (Abu Dawud 332, Bayhaqi 27)"
"19882","(19882) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I asked Ibn Sirin, I said: A man wants to invade, so he helps? He said: Muslims continue to entertain one another."
"19883","(19883) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Nasir, that Al-Rabi’ used to take the prizes and put them in Poor people."
"19884","(19884) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, that he was given the commandment on the day he conquered something. So he accepted it."
"19885","(19885) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Ikrimah, Al-Aswad, and Masruq that they disliked it. Al-Ja'il, and that is in the Resurrection."
"19886","(19886) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq, that he hated the Ja’il."
"19887","(19887) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, who said: Al-Nu’man ibn Abi Ayash and Ibn Qusayt and Amr ibn Alqamiya take the prizes and leave."
"19888","(1988) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It was Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid. He becomes friends with a man, then breaks up with him."
"19889","(19889) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: There are no days in which good deeds are more beloved to God than these days, meaning days. The ten, they said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, not even jihad in the way of God? He said: Not even jihad in the way of God, unless a man goes out with his life and his wealth and does not return with anything of that. (Bukhari 969. Abu Dawud 2430)"
"19890","(19890) Ghandar narrated to me, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ya’qub, who said: Whoever heard his message informed me. Al-Islami from across the Balkh River, and he says: There is no livelihood except the shine of horses."
"19891","(19891) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Masoud Uqba. Ibn Amr said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a mottled camel, and he said: O Messenger of God, this is in For the sake of God, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: You will have seven hundred percent of it on the Day of Resurrection. muzzled\n(Muslim 1506. Ahmad 121)"
"19892","(19892) Affan told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Abu Talha, he said: I raised my head on the day Uhud, so I started to look, and I did not see any of the people but slumbering under his covers from drowsiness. (Bukhari 4068 and Tirmidhi 3007)"
"19893","(19893) Affan told us, Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zubayr, like him."
"19894","(19894) Zayd bin Harun told us, Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Sa’sa bin Muawiyah told me, he said: I met Abu Dharr, so I said: Tell me a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: There is no Muslim who spends of his wealth on two wives in the path of God but that the jinn will quickly veil him. Al-Hasan used to say: Two pairs of his wealth: two dinars, two dirhams, two slaves, and two of each thing.\n(Ibn Hibban 4643, Ahmad 5/151)"
"19895","(19895) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Maimun bin Mihran, who said: Abu Bakr was He wanted to send a mission to appoint people, and when he had enough of the number he wanted, he would equip them with what he had, but it was not The gifts were made obligatory during the reign of Abu Bakr."
"19896","(19896) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Saad bin Iyad, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He was of little speech and of little speech. When he was ordered to fight, he raised his hair, and he was one of the most powerful of people."
"19897","(19897) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Rafi’, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And peace be upon him: Conquer, you will recover, and you will gain spoils."
"19898","(19898) Yazeed bin Harun told us, Hisham Al-Dastawai told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Azraq, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: God With a single arrow, three jinn will enter: the one who made it and expects goodness in his work, the one who shoots it, and the one who supplies it. And he said: Shoot and ride, and that you shoot is more beloved to me than that you ride, and everything that a Muslim man entertains with is invalid unless he throws it. With his bow, and the training of his horse, and the playing with him of his family, they are of the truth. (Tirmidhi 1437. Ahmad 4/148)"
"19899","(19899) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Samir al-Ra’aniy, that he heard Abu Ali al-Tajibi said that he heard Abu Rayhani say: We attacked with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we were struck by cold. One night, I saw the man digging the pit, then entering it, and placing his shield on it, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Who will guard us at night? Then a man from the Ansar said: I. He said: Who are you from? So he went to him and prayed for his well-being, then said: Who will guard us at night? I said: I am. He said: Who are you from? So I said: Abu Rayhani, so he supplicated for me without supplicating for the Ansari, then he said: The Fire was forbidden to three eyes: one eye that walked away. For the sake of God, and an eye that wept or shed tears out of fear of God.\n Muhammad bin Samir remained silent about the third, and did not mention it. (Bukhari 2748. Ahmad 4/134)"
"19900","(19900) Waki’ narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Misra, and Al-Mughirah bin Shibl, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, He said: When Salman came from a campaign, he would come to Al-Qadisiyah, and when he came from Hajj, he would come to Medina as a conqueror."
"19901","(19901) Muawiyah bin Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever is spoken in the way of God, and God knows best who is spoken in His way, will come. On the Day of Resurrection, his wound will be the same as his appearance on the day he was wounded. (Bukhari 2371, Muslim 1496)"
"19902","(19902) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, Laith bin Saad told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Asama, on the authority of Al-Walid Ibn Abi Al-Walid, on the authority of Othman Ibn Abdullah Ibn Suraqi, on the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, he says: Whoever shades the head of a raider, God will shade him on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever prepares a raider until he is independent will have a similarity. His reward until he dies, or returns, and whoever builds a mosque in which the name of God is mentioned, God will build a house for him in it. Heaven\n(Ahmad 20. Ibn Hibban 4628)"
"19903","(19903) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, Zuhair bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Sahl bin Hanif, that Sahl narrated to him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever helps a mujahid in For the sake of God, or as a debtor in your hardship, or as a burden on his neck, God will shade him on the Day when there will be no shade but His shade. (Ahmad 3/487 Hakim 89)"
"19904","(19904) Waki’ narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Zayd bin Khalid Al-Junni, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever breaks the fast for a fasting person, or provides for a pilgrim, or a pilgrim, or succeeds him among his family, will have Similar to their wages without detracting from their wages in any way. (Tirmidhi 807. Ahmad 4/114)"
"19905","(19905) Zaid bin Harun told us, Hisham Al-Dastawai told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Aamer Al-Uqaili, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: It was presented to me first. Three of my nation will enter Paradise: a martyr, an owned slave who was not distracted by the slavery of this world from obeying his Lord, and a poor person. A chaste person with dependents.\n(Tirmidhi 1452. Ahmad 2/425)"
"19906","(19906) Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Muammar said: Makhoul was facing the qiblah, then He swears ten oaths: Conquest is your duty, then he says: If you wish, I can add more to you."
"19907","(19907) Muhammad bin Abi Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Dawud said to me: I said to Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab: I may know that Conquest is obligatory for all people. He said: Then he remained silent. He said: Then he said: I knew that if he denied what I said, he would explain it to me. So I said to Saeed. Ibn Al-Musayyab: Are you equipped? He will not rebuke me except that until I am settled. He said: I have sufficed for you."
"19908","(19908) Ibn al-Mubarak told us, he said: I said to Ata: Is invasion obligatory? He said: He and Amr bin Dinar: We did not know."
"19909","(19909) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Amara ibn al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, who said: Omar said: The bonds of faith are four: Prayer, zakat, jihad, and trustworthiness."
"19910","(19910) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Salla, Hudhayfy said: Islam is eight chapters. : Prayer is an arrow, zakat is an arrow, jihad is an arrow, Hajj is an arrow, fasting Ramadan is an arrow, and enjoining what is right is an arrow. An arrow, and forbidding evil is an arrow, and he who has no arrow has been disappointed. (Bazzar 2928, Darqutni 628)"
"19911","(19911) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Aisha, she said: If any of you feels He is cowardly himself, so he will not fight against you."
"19912","(19912) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Atiyya, the client of Banu Amir, on the authority of Zayd bin Bishr al-Saksaki said: I came to Medina and entered upon Abdullah bin Omar, and a man from the people of Iraq came to him. He said: O Abdullah bin Omar, why do you perform Hajj and Umrah when you have given up fighting for the sake of God? He said: Woe to you, faith is built on five things: you worship God, perform prayer, pay zakat, perform Hajj, and fast Ramadan. He said: He responded to me. He said: O servant of God, you worship God, perform prayer, pay zakat, perform Hajj, and fast Ramadan. This is what he said to us. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then jihad is good. (Bukhari 8: Muslim 22)"
"19913","(19913) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar used to fight by himself and carry on a mount. He believes that jihad in the path of God is the best of deeds after prayer."
"19914","(19914) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Umayyah al-Shami, who said: Makhoul and Raja’ ibn Haywah used to choose the bartender, not He leaves her."
"19915","(19915) Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, Ali bin Salih told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: The one who prevails in the way of God is better than the one who is killed."
"19916","Abu Abd al-Rahman Buqiy bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shayba al-Absi told us, He said:\n(19916) Muhammad bin Fudayl al-Dhabi told us, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Adiy bin Hatim, who said: I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I said: We are a people who hunt with these dogs. He said: If you send your trained dogs and mention the name of May God bless her, then eat from what they have seized upon you, and if they kill, unless they eat, but if they eat, then do not eat, for I fear that It is only that he kept it on his own, and if other dogs come into contact with it, then do not eat it. (Bukhari 5483, Abu Dawud 2842)"
"19917","(19917) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: If you send your tame dog and it eats from it, and you do not realize its slaughter, then do not eat from it, and if you do not He ate from it, and I found that he had died, so eat."
"19918","(19918) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Ibn Abbas said: If you send your dog and he takes The game and he ate from it, do not eat, as he only kept it for himself, and if he did not eat from it, then eat, then he only kept it for you. And if he kills"
"19919","(19919) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If you send your dog and he eats, do not eat, for he only kept it for himself."
"19920","(19920) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: If he eats from his hunt, strike him, for he is not... With a teacher"
"19921","(19921) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If a dog eats from game, it is not With a teacher"
"19922","(19922) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If the dog eats, do not eat."
"19923","(19923) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal Al-Ta’i, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: I asked him about He caught the dog and said: Protect him and send him away, and mention the name of God, and eat whatever he catches from you, unless he eats it."
"19924","(19924) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a dog eats from game, do not eat it."
"19925","(19925) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, about the dog eating, He said: He only kept it for himself, and he did not hold it for you, so do not eat."
"19926","(19926) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He is dead."
"19927","(19927) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: If he eats, do not eat."
"19928","(19928) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, who said: If you send your trained dog and mention the name of By God, eat, even if he kills. Sufyan said: I doubt Al-Bazi."
"19929","(19929) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; What about a dog eating from his catch? He said: Do not eat."
"19930","(19930) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he eats, do not eat."
"19931","(19931) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If the dog eats, do not eat."
"19932","(19932) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibn Abd al-Ala, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafli, who said: If you send your dog And I mentioned the name of God upon him, so eat what he did not eat."
"19933","(19933) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, and Abu Burda, who said: A dog hunts, if it eats, then it does not. You eat"
"19934","(19934) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; Concerning a dog, if it is trained and catches a kill: if it eats from it, do not eat it, but if it kills and catches you, then eat it."
"19935","(19935) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Dawud told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: If you send your dog and he eats, it is only He kept it to himself and did not eat, for he did not learn what I taught him."
"19936","(19936) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaid, who said: Aban bin Salih narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Salma Umm Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If a man sends a hunter, and mentions the name of By God, let him eat what he has not eaten. (Royani 698)"
"19937","(19937) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Abu Tha’labah al-Khushani, and on the authority of al-Walid. Ibn Abi Malik, on the authority of God forbid, that he heard Abu Thalabb Al-Khushani say: I said: O Messenger of God, we are the people of Sidon. He said: If you send your dog, and mention the name of God upon him, and he catches you, then eat. He said: I said: And if he kills? He said: Even if he kills.\n(Bukhari 5478 and Muslim 1532) (2) Whoever permits him to eat it and eats it."
"19938","(19938) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Eat, even if he eats."
"19939","(19939) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, Saad, and Salman; They did not see any harm in him eating from his own game."
"19940","(19940) Abdullah bin Numayr and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, On the authority of Humaid bin Malik, he said: I asked Saad bin Abi Waqqas: We have predatory dogs that we send to hunt and they eat. And it will be cut off, so he said: Even if only a few remain."
"19941","(19941) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: I asked him about the dog. He was sent to hunt, and he said: Eat, and if he ate two-thirds of it, I said: On whose behalf? He said: On the authority of Salman."
"19942","(19942) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, he said: Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: If you were sent If your dog eats, then eat, and if he eats two-thirds of it."
"19943","(19943) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Salman, who said: If he eats Two-thirds of it, then the remaining third."
"19944","(19944) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Nafi`, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Anyone who catches a dog eats from His prey"
"19945","(19945) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said to him: If he eats The dog ate, even if only a few remained."
"19946","(19946) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, who said: I said: O Messenger of God, we We are a people who hunt. What is lawful for us and what is forbidden to us? He said: It is permissible for you (whatever you have learned of the preys, by chaining them, you will teach them from what God has taught you, so eat of what they have captured for you.) And mention the name of God upon him.) He said: I said: Even if he is killed? He said: And if he kills, he said: And if other dogs come into contact with it, do not eat it until you know that it was your dog that took it.\n(Abu Dawud 2845, Tirmidhi 1470)"
"19947","(19947) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Jamil bin Zayd, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about hunting dogs, and he said: Aren't you an imitator? He said: I said: Yes, I started driving it? He said: Does she drive? He said: I said: Some of them I lead, and some of them follow me. He said: If you see hunting, and take off your dog, and mention the name of God Then eat whatever it catches, and as for the following dog, if it catches you, do not bother with it, unless you find it alive and slaughter it, or else If a dog you did not send prey on him, that is forbidden."
"19948","(19948) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, who said: I asked Al-Qasim about a man who sends a trained dog and he takes it. The hunter kills him and finds with him untrained dogs. He said: If he knew that his trained dog killed him. Let him eat, and if he is in doubt, he does not know. Perhaps someone other than the dog has swayed him, so he will not eat."
"19949","(19949) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the dog that is not trained responds to the dog that is trained Sidon has spoiled."
"19950","(19950) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Ata’ about a man who forgets to name his dog. So he kills, he said: he eats."
"19951","(19951) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Harmala, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab; Concerning a man who sends his dog and forgets to call it, he said: There is nothing wrong with it."
"19952","(19952) Asbat narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah ibn Muslim, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He was asked about a man who sent His dog, but he did not name it. He said: The Muslim has the name of God Almighty in it."
"19953","(19953) Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: If he sent his dog and forgot to name it Let him eat."
"19954","(19954) Abd al-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders; Concerning a man who sends his dog and his falcon and forgets to say the name of God and they kill him. He said: He eats you."
"19955","(19955) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If you shot an arrow, and did not say the name, then mentioned Before you kill the game, then you name it, then kill it and eat it, and the dog is like that."
"19956","(19956) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: If a dog is let loose and its owner is not aware of it, then he said after The dog seeks to hunt: In the name of God, and the dog hunts, let him eat."
"19957","(19957) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: If you send your dog, or Your arrow and you forgot to say the name, that is, when you sent it, then you said the name before you took it, so do not eat until you say the name. You send him"
"19958","(19958) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said; Concerning a man who threw stones and forgot to mention the name of God, he said: He saw no harm in it."
"19959","(19959) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Harmala, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: I said: I threw my stone and forgot. If my name is given, he said: So mention the name of God and eat."
"19960","(19960) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who sent his dog to hunt and it took someone else, he said: There is no harm in it."
"19961","(19961) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I asked him about a man who shoots a game and hits someone else. He said: He eats it"
"19962","(19962) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who shot a shot and said the name of Allah upon it and it hit someone else, he said: There is no problem."
"19963","(19963) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Like him"
"19964","(19964) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, about a man who shoots game and does not intentionally hit one of them. He said: He eats when he mentions the name of God."
"19965","(19965) Abdullah bin Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, he said: His leaders narrated to me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, about a dog. The polytheist, he said: It is only his kashfirah, he said: Al-Zuhri said: If you are fishing with it, then there is no problem."
"19966","(19966) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that he hated hunting the dog of the Magians and the Jews. And the Christian."
"19967","(19967) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He does not hunt with the dog of the Magians, nor does he eat from His hunting"
"19968","(19968) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that it was disliked for a Muslim to seek help. He uses the dog of the Magi to hunt with it, and he sees no harm in using the dog of the Jew and Christian to hunt. With it"
"19969","(19969) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he was a hunter. The dog of the Magi."
"19970","(19970) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: His dog is like a knife."
"19971","(19971) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: There is no harm in the hunting of a Jew. And the Christians and their sacrifices, and there is no good in the hunt of the Magians and their sacrifices."
"19972","(19972) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: There is no good in hunting. The Magi, not his fawn, nor his dog."
"19973","(19973) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid and Ata’ that they hated the hunting of a dog. The Magi"
"19974","(19974) Abd al-Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his commanders, on the authority of al-Hasan, that he was reluctant to A man borrows the dog of a Magian, a Christian, or a Jew and hunts with it and says: You did not know."
"19975","(19975) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, that he hated hunting the dog of the Magians."
"19976","(19976) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, that he hated a hunter. The Magi"
"19977","(19977) I heard a man saying: I heard Sufyan who hated hunting the dogs of the Magians until he took away their teachings. The Muslim"
"19978","(19978) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: I told him: The Magian is being sent to Bazi? He said: Yes."
"19979","(19979) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the Magian bird, he said: It is not eaten."
"19980","(19980) Ali bin Hisham and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Isa bin Asim, on the authority of Ali, that He hated the hunter of his falcon and his falcon."
"19981","(19981) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: There is no good in his falcon, nor In his country"
"19982","(19982) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, that he hated the hunting of a falcon and a falcon."
"19983","(19983) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If you take the game and there is a dead animal in it and it dies in your hand, then do not You eat it"
"19984","(19984) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’ that he threw a stone at Dibiyya and it took Abdullah treated him by coming with him to slaughter him, but he died in his hands before he slaughtered him, so he threw him."
"19985","(19985) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you were in the hunt to hunt, he would outpace you. By itself, there is no harm in eating it, but if you wait for it and it dies, then do not eat it."
"19986","(19986) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked the ruling about a man who overtakes the hunt, and he kills it. So he would leave the dog until it killed him. He said: He would not eat it."
"19987","(19987) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Abu Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who sent his dog to hunt a hunter, and it overtook the hunter with a spear in it, and it died in his hands. He said: If the dog He is troubled, let him eat."
"19988","(19988) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Mu’awiyah ibn Qur’a, who said: One of them used to send His dog calls him, but he does not see hunting, so if he hunts, he will eat it."
"19989","(19989) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Ata’ about dogs that escape from their cages and are killed. He said: There is no problem with that."
"19990","(19990) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Marouf, who said: We went out with dogs and met Ibn Umar, and he said: If you send him, then name him. May God bless her and say: Oh God, guide her breasts."
"19991","(19991) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Zuhair ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, that his father was He sent his dogs and said: Oh God, guide her breasts."
"19992","(19992) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Adiy ibn Hatim, who said: If he drinks of his blood, he will not Eat, for he did not know what I taught him."
"19993","(19993) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he eats, do not eat, and if he drinks, then eat."
"19994","(19994) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If he eats, do not eat, and if he drinks, do not eat."
"19995","(19995) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he eats, then eat, and if he drinks, then eat."
"19996","(19996) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said about birds and fawns. And falcons and other things. And whatever you have reached its slaughter time is yours, and as long as you have not reached its slaughter time, do not eat it."
"19997","(19997) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The dog and the baz are one and the same thing. All hunting."
"19998","(19998) Ibn Aliyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Haytham, on the authority of Talha ibn Musarrif, he said: He said: Khaythamah bin Abdul Rahman: This is what I have proven to you. Indeed, hawks and falcons are among the raptors."
"19999","(19999) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he did not see harm in hunting the goshawk. And the falcon."
"20000","(20000) Muadh narrated to us, saying: Ash’ath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say about the falcon and the falcon that they are in his abode. The dog"
"20001","(20001) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Mujahid: {And what of the preys you have known to be chained} He said: Of birds. And dogs."
"20002","(20002) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, who said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, about the hunting of Al-Bazi, and he said: Whatever it catches you, eat it. (Abu Dawud 2845. Ahmad 4/257)"
"20003","(20003) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Sa’id, who said: If he eats, do not eat."
"20004","(20004) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of al-Shu`abi, they said: Everyone who hunts Al-Bazi, even if he eats."
"20005","(20005) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of something alcoholic about the falcon and the dog: if he got some of it, or ate from it. So eat, even if he eats."
"20006","(20006) Yazeed bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak about the dog if it was a guide and it struck a hunter, or The Bazi ate, so do not eat."
"20007","(20007) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hammad, who said: If the bird is plucked, or eaten, then eat. Your teaching is to return to you."
"20008","(20008) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir and Al-Hakam, who said: If you send your falcon, Or your bazīk, then you invited him and he came to you, and that is his knowledge. So if you send for a hunter and he eats, then eat."
"20009","(2009) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Al-Furat, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab On the authority of Salman, he said: If you send your dog or your goat, then eat, and if he eats a third of it."
"20010","(20010) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar ibn al-Walid al-Shinni, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: If a goshawk or a falcon eats, do not eat."
"20011","(20011) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and ‘Ata’ regarding the bazi and the falcon: he eats. Ata’ said: if he eats So do not eat. Al-Hasan said: Eat."
"20012","(20012) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that he did not see hunting. The leopard is mighty."
"20013","(20013) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The leopard is one of the raptors."
"20014","(20014) Abdul Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Hammad, who said: There is no harm in hunting a leopard."
"20015","(20015) Rawad bin Al-Jarrah told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: There is no harm in hunting a leopard."
"20016","(20016) Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Fahd and the Shaheen are in the same position as the dog."
"20017","(2017) Al-Muharbibi told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated to hunt dogs. And the leopard, if it eats from it and sees no harm in hunting the falcon if it eats, because the dog and the leopard are harmful, and the falcon does not He is harmed."
"20018","(2018) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: There is no harm in the Magi catching fish."
"20019","(20019) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Eat fish, and whoever catches them will not harm you."
"20020","(20020) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It is not eaten from the hunt of the Magians except Whales"
"20021","(20021) Omar bin Ayyub told us, on the authority of Mughirah bin Ziyad, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: All the game of the sea whatever it catches The Jew, the Christian, and the Magian."
"20022","(20022) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in the Magi catching fish."
"20023","(20023) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Harun bin Saad, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Everyone who Magi, Christian and Jew fishing."
"20024","(20024) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Al Hassan, And Ibn Sirin said that they saw nothing wrong with the Magians catching fish."
"20025","(20025) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: I asked him about The Magian catches fish. He said: His catch is clever."
"20026","(20026) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, that he saw no harm in hunting the Magians. It means for fish."
"20027","(20027) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, who said: Do not eat from the catch of the Magians except fish and locusts."
"20028","(20028) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’ and Al-Nakha’i, that they did not see any harm. By the Magi hunting for fish."
"20029","(20029) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Their catch is eaten in the sea. Their game in the land shall not be eaten."
"20030","(20030) Waki’ and Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Isa bin Asim, on the authority of Ali, that He hated the Magians hunting for fish."
"20031","(20031) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I asked him about the hunt of the Magians, his thoughts."
"20032","(20032) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: Do not eat from the hunt of the Magians called Sami. Or did he not name him?"
"20033","(20033) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Abu Razin, who said: A man came to The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a rabbit, and he said: I threw a rabbit, but I was unable to search for it until the night overtook me, and I did not. He continued on it until the morning came and found it with an arrow in it. He said: Have you become silent, or have you died? He said: No, but I slept. He said: The night is a great creation among God’s creation. No one can estimate its destiny except the One who created it. Perhaps he helped in killing her. Something we rejected. (Abu Dawud 383)"
"20034","(20034) Ibn Numayr and Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abu Razin, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a similar manner. (Bayhaqi 241)"
"20035","(20035) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, who said: A man came to Abu Darda’ and said: I am an Armenian. The game will disappear from me, then I will find my arrow in it and I will recognize it from tomorrow. He said: As for me, I was eating it."
"20036","(20036) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Dhudhail, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas A black slave asked him, and he said to him: O Abu Abbas, I shoot game, so fast and sleep, so he said: As long as I fast, eat. And whatever it grows, do not eat."
"20037","(20037) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, with something similar to the hadith of Hafs."
"20038","(20038) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: If he throws a shot, then finds Let him eat his arrow from tomorrow."
"20039","(20039) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amer; Concerning a man shooting game and missing it, he said: If you find him, he did not fall into water, nor did he fall from a mountain, nor did he Eat seven of it, then eat."
"20040","(20040) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, who said: If you find If you contribute to it the next day, then you recognize it, so there is no problem."
